-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Parts VII to X -- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds shares in a corporation under the Canada Business
-- Corporations Act: an incorporator, a director or officer, or a shareholder (including a minority
-- shareholder). The questions ask what the Act lets that person do, what it requires of them, what they may
-- require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person
-- would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every question calls one layer-1 rule.
-- GENERATED by inputs/work/gen/seat_build.py from gen/seat_spec.py; the inputs, their types and the order of the
-- call are read from the compiled layer-1 modules.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes or no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own choices --
-- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc. A fact that may be absent in the rule (a MAYBE) is
-- asked as two inputs, "yes or no" and "the value", and the question builds the MAYBE from them; a list of dates
-- or numbers is asked as three inputs (a date is repeated, and a number is 0, if fewer apply). Judgments the Act leaves to someone
-- else (a court, the directors, the articles) are asked as facts the person states, never answered conditionally.
-- NOT COVERED. A question whose answer is a MAYBE returns NOTHING when the Act does not answer it for the facts given:
-- NOTHING means "the Act is silent here", never "no". The cases file asserts NOTHING for such facts.
-- A question that asks about the corporation's or another party's side of a relation takes that party's acts as
-- plain inputs; there is no seat for the Director, a court, a registrar or any official.


§ `Securities, certificates, registers and transfers (Part VII, ss 48 to 81)`

§§ `What the corporation owes a security holder: certificates (s 49)`

-- s 49(1). A security holder may opt for a security certificate or a non-transferable written acknowledgement of their right to obtain one.
@export What may I demand from the corporation for the securities I hold (s 49(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a security holder of the corporation in respect of securities of the corporation held by them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a security holder of the corporation in respect of securities of the corporation held by them?
      `the holder opts for a security certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder opts for a security certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a security holder may be given under s 49(1)`
DECIDE `What may I demand from the corporation for the securities I hold` IS `what the corporation must give the security holder at their option within s 49(1)` `the person is a security holder of the corporation in respect of securities of the corporation held by them` `the holder opts for a security certificate`

@export May the corporation charge me a fee for issuing a certificate (s 49(2))?
GIVEN `the certificate is issued in respect of a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is issued in respect of a transfer?
      `the fee the corporation charges in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee the corporation charges in dollars?
      `the prescribed maximum fee in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed maximum fee in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation charge me a fee for issuing a certificate` IS `the corporation may charge the fee within s 49(2)` `the certificate is issued in respect of a transfer` `the fee the corporation charges in dollars` `the prescribed maximum fee in dollars`

@export Need the corporation issue a separate certificate to each of us who hold jointly (s 49(3))?
GIVEN `the securities are held jointly by several persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the securities are held jointly by several persons?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Need the corporation issue a separate certificate to each of us who hold jointly` IF `the corporation need not issue more than one security certificate within s 49(3)` `the securities are held jointly by several persons`

@export Is delivery of a certificate to one of us enough where we hold jointly (s 49(3))?
GIVEN `the securities are held jointly by several persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the securities are held jointly by several persons?
      `the certificate is delivered to at least one of the joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is delivered to at least one of the joint holders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is delivery of a certificate to one of us enough where we hold jointly` IF `delivery to one joint holder is sufficient delivery to all within s 49(3)` `the securities are held jointly by several persons` `the certificate is delivered to at least one of the joint holders`

@export Is our security certificate signed as the Act requires (s 49(4))?
GIVEN `the signature of a director or officer of the corporation is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature of a director or officer of the corporation is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced?
      `the signature of a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation or of an individual on their behalf is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature of a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation or of an individual on their behalf is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced?
      `the signature of a trustee who certifies the certificate in accordance with a trust indenture is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature of a trustee who certifies the certificate in accordance with a trust indenture is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our security certificate signed as the Act requires` IF `a security certificate is signed as required within s 49(4)` `the signature of a director or officer of the corporation is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` `the signature of a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation or of an individual on their behalf is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` `the signature of a trustee who certifies the certificate in accordance with a trust indenture is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced`

@export May the corporation issue a certificate that bears the printed signature of someone who has since left office (s 49(6))?
GIVEN `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation issue a certificate that bears the printed signature of someone who has since left office` IF `the corporation may issue the certificate within s 49(6)` `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person`

@export Does our share certificate state what it must on its face (s 49(7))?
GIVEN `the face states the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the face states the name of the corporation?
      `the face states the words "Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act" or "subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the face states the words "Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act" or "subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act"?
      `the face states the name of the person to whom the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the face states the name of the person to whom the certificate was issued?
      `the face states the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the face states the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our share certificate state what it must on its face` IF `a share certificate states what it must on its face within s 49(7)` `the face states the name of the corporation` `the face states the words "Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act" or "subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act"` `the face states the name of the person to whom the certificate was issued` `the face states the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents`

@export Is a restriction, lien or agreement that is not noted on my certificate ineffective against me as a transferee (s 49(8))?
GIVEN `the security was issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security was issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act?
      `the kind of item` IS A `Kind of item that must be noted on a certificate under s 49(8)` @desc What is the kind of item?
      `the transferee has actual knowledge of the item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transferee has actual knowledge of the item?
      `the item or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the item or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a restriction, lien or agreement that is not noted on my certificate ineffective against me as a transferee` IF `the item is ineffective against the transferee within s 49(8)` `the security was issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act` `the kind of item` `the transferee has actual knowledge of the item` `the item or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate`

@export May the corporation restrict the transfer or ownership of its shares (s 49(9))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is a distributing corporation?
      `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person?
      `the restriction is a constraint permitted under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the restriction is a constraint permitted under section 174?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation restrict the transfer or ownership of its shares` IS `the corporation may have the restriction on transfer or ownership within s 49(9)` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` `the restriction is a constraint permitted under section 174`

@export Must a constraint on who may own our shares be noted on the certificate (s 49(10))?
GIVEN `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a law prescribed by the regulations for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a law prescribed by the regulations for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control?
      `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation to comply with a law prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation to comply with a law prescribed by the regulations?
      `the certificate evidences a share that is subject to the constraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate evidences a share that is subject to the constraint?
      `the day the certificate is issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the certificate is issued?
      `the day the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a constraint on who may own our shares be noted on the certificate` IF `the constraint must be noted conspicuously on the certificate within s 49(10)` `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a law prescribed by the regulations for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation to comply with a law prescribed by the regulations` `the certificate evidences a share that is subject to the constraint` `the day the certificate is issued` `the day the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act`

@export Does a failure to note the constraint invalidate my share (s 49(11))?
GIVEN `there was a failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection 49(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there was a failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection 49(10)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a failure to note the constraint invalidate my share` IS `the failure to note invalidates a share or certificate or makes the constraint ineffective within s 49(11)` `there was a failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection 49(10)`

@export Does our share certificate give the particulars of each class and series (s 49(13))?
GIVEN `the corporation is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series?
      `the certificate states legibly the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states legibly the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when it is issued?
      `the certificate states legibly that the class or series has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached and that the corporation will furnish a full copy of their text on demand and without charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states legibly that the class or series has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached and that the corporation will furnish a full copy of their text on demand and without charge?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our share certificate give the particulars of each class and series` IF `a share certificate gives the particulars of the class or series within s 49(13)` `the corporation is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series` `the certificate states legibly the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when it is issued` `the certificate states legibly that the class or series has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached and that the corporation will furnish a full copy of their text on demand and without charge`

@export Must the corporation give me a copy of the rights attached to a class of shares on demand (s 49(14))?
GIVEN `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)?
      `the person asking is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person asking is a shareholder?
      `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shareholder demands a full copy of the text?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give me a copy of the rights attached to a class of shares on demand` IF `the corporation must furnish a full copy of the text on demand within s 49(14)` `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` `the person asking is a shareholder` `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text`

@export What is the most the corporation may charge me for that copy (s 49(14))?
GIVEN `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)?
      `the person asking is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person asking is a shareholder?
      `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shareholder demands a full copy of the text?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the corporation may charge me for that copy` IS `the most the corporation may charge for the copy in dollars within s 49(14)` `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` `the person asking is a shareholder` `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text`

@export May the corporation issue a certificate or scrip certificates for a fractional share (s 49(15))?
GIVEN `the share is a fractional share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the share is a fractional share?
      `the certificate or each scrip certificate is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate or each scrip certificate is in registered form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation issue a certificate or scrip certificates for a fractional share` IF `the corporation may issue a certificate or scrip certificates for the fractional share within s 49(15)` `the share is a fractional share` `the certificate or each scrip certificate is in registered form`

@export How many full-share certificates may I receive in exchange for my scrip certificates (s 49(15))?
GIVEN `the fractions of a share that the holder's scrip certificates represent, added together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fractions of a share that the holder's scrip certificates represent, added together?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many full-share certificates may I receive in exchange for my scrip certificates` IS `the number of full-share certificates the holder may receive in exchange within s 49(15)` `the fractions of a share that the holder's scrip certificates represent, added together`

@export Must the corporation exchange my bearer or scrip certificate for a registered one (s 49(15.1))?
GIVEN `the holder requests an exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder requests an exchange?
      `the certificate is for a fractional share or is a scrip certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is for a fractional share or is a scrip certificate?
      `the certificate is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is in bearer form?
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the certificate was issued?
      `the day subsection 49(15.1) came into force` IS A DATE @desc What is the day subsection 49(15.1) came into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation exchange my bearer or scrip certificate for a registered one` IF `the corporation must issue a registered-form certificate in exchange within s 49(15.1)` `the holder requests an exchange` `the certificate is for a fractional share or is a scrip certificate` `the certificate is in bearer form` `the day the certificate was issued` `the day subsection 49(15.1) came into force`

@export Has my scrip certificate become void (s 49(16))?
GIVEN `the directors attached a condition that unexchanged scrip certificates become void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors attached a condition that unexchanged scrip certificates become void?
      `the scrip certificate was exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before the specified date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the scrip certificate was exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before the specified date?
      `the specified date` IS A DATE @desc What is the specified date?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my scrip certificate become void` IF `the scrip certificate has become void within s 49(16)(a)` `the directors attached a condition that unexchanged scrip certificates become void` `the scrip certificate was exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before the specified date` `the specified date` `the day asked about`

@export What is my rateable share of the proceeds of shares sold for scrip holders (s 49(16))?
GIVEN `the proceeds in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the proceeds in dollars?
      `the scrip certificates the holder holds, as fractions of a share, added together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the scrip certificates the holder holds, as fractions of a share, added together?
      `all the scrip certificates outstanding, as fractions of a share, added together` IS A NUMBER @desc Added together as fractions of a share, how many scrip certificates are outstanding?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my rateable share of the proceeds of shares sold for scrip holders` IS `the holder's rateable share of the proceeds in dollars within s 49(16)(b)` `the proceeds in dollars` `the scrip certificates the holder holds, as fractions of a share, added together` `all the scrip certificates outstanding, as fractions of a share, added together`

@export Am I barred from voting and from dividends on my fractional share (s 49(17))?
GIVEN `the person holds a fractional share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person holds a fractional share?
      `the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares?
      `the articles of the corporation otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles of the corporation otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from voting and from dividends on my fractional share` IF `the holder of the fractional share is barred from voting and from dividends within s 49(17)` `the person holds a fractional share` `the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares` `the articles of the corporation otherwise provide`

@export Am I barred from voting and from dividends on my scrip certificate (s 49(18))?
GIVEN `the person holds a scrip certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person holds a scrip certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from voting and from dividends on my scrip certificate` IF `the holder of the scrip certificate is barred from voting and from dividends within s 49(18)` `the person holds a scrip certificate`

§§ `Registers and who the corporation treats as the holder (ss 50 and 51)`

@export Does our securities register contain what the Act requires (s 50(1))?
GIVEN `the register records the securities the corporation issued in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the register records the securities the corporation issued in registered form?
      `for each class or series the register shows the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that for each class or series the register shows the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder?
      `for each class or series the register shows the number of securities held by each security holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that for each class or series the register shows the number of securities held by each security holder?
      `for each class or series the register shows the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that for each class or series the register shows the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our securities register contain what the Act requires` IF `the corporation maintains the securities register as required within s 50(1)` `the register records the securities the corporation issued in registered form` `for each class or series the register shows the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder` `for each class or series the register shows the number of securities held by each security holder` `for each class or series the register shows the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security`

@export Is our central securities register kept in a permitted place (s 50(3))?
GIVEN `the central register is kept at the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the central register is kept at the registered office of the corporation?
      `the central register is kept at another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the central register is kept at another place in Canada designated by the directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our central securities register kept in a permitted place` IF `the central securities register is kept at a permitted place within s 50(3)` `the central register is kept at the registered office of the corporation` `the central register is kept at another place in Canada designated by the directors`

@export Is our branch securities register kept in a permitted place (s 50(3))?
GIVEN `the branch register is kept at a place designated by the directors, in or out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the branch register is kept at a place designated by the directors, in or out of Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our branch securities register kept in a permitted place` IF `a branch securities register is kept at a permitted place within s 50(3)` `the branch register is kept at a place designated by the directors, in or out of Canada`

@export Is my transfer complete once it is registered in the central or a branch register (s 50(4))?
GIVEN `the issue or transfer is registered in the central securities register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issue or transfer is registered in the central securities register?
      `the issue or transfer is registered in a branch securities register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issue or transfer is registered in a branch securities register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my transfer complete once it is registered in the central or a branch register` IF `the registration is complete and valid for all purposes within s 50(4)` `the issue or transfer is registered in the central securities register` `the issue or transfer is registered in a branch securities register`

@export May the corporation refuse to produce an instrument it has cancelled or that has expired (s 50(7))?
GIVEN `the form of the instrument` IS A `Form of an instrument under s 50(7)` @desc What is the form of the instrument?
      `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the instrument was cancelled? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired? (yes or no)
      `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the instrument expired? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation refuse to produce an instrument it has cancelled or that has expired` IF `the corporation, its agent or a trustee need not produce the instrument within s 50(7)` `the form of the instrument` `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was as the rule reads it` `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export May the corporation treat the registered owner as the only person entitled to my security (s 51(1))?
GIVEN `the person is the registered owner of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the registered owner of the security?
      `section 134, 135 or 138 limits the treatment of the registered owner as exclusively entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that section 134, 135 or 138 limits the treatment of the registered owner as exclusively entitled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation treat the registered owner as the only person entitled to my security` IF `the corporation may treat the registered owner as exclusively entitled within s 51(1)` `the person is the registered owner of the security` `section 134, 135 or 138 limits the treatment of the registered owner as exclusively entitled`

@export Must or may the corporation treat me as a registered holder because of the capacity in which I act (s 51(2))?
GIVEN `the articles of the corporation restrict the right to transfer its securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles of the corporation restrict the right to transfer its securities?
      `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)` @desc What is the capacity of the person?
      `the person furnishes evidence as described in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person furnishes evidence as described in subsection 77(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the corporation must or may do under s 51(2)`
DECIDE `Must or may the corporation treat me as a registered holder because of the capacity in which I act` IS `whether the corporation must or may treat the person as a registered security holder within s 51(2)` `the articles of the corporation restrict the right to transfer its securities` `the capacity of the person` `the person furnishes evidence as described in subsection 77(4)`

@export Must the corporation treat me as entitled to exercise the rights because ownership has passed to me by law (s 51(3))?
GIVEN `ownership of the security devolves on the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that ownership of the security devolves on the person by operation of law?
      `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)` @desc What is the capacity of the person?
      `the security is not registered in the person's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is not registered in the person's name?
      `the person furnishes proof of their authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person furnishes proof of their authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation treat me as entitled to exercise the rights because ownership has passed to me by law` IF `the corporation must treat the person as entitled to exercise the rights within s 51(3)` `ownership of the security devolves on the person by operation of law` `the capacity of the person` `the security is not registered in the person's name` `the person furnishes proof of their authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of the security`

@export Need the corporation inquire into a duty owed to a third person by a registered holder (s 51(4))?
GIVEN `the duty is owed to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the duty is owed to a third person?
      `the duty is owed by a registered holder of a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the duty is owed by a registered holder of a security of the corporation?
      `the duty is owed by a person the corporation treats, as permitted or required by section 51, as the owner or registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the duty is owed by a person the corporation treats, as permitted or required by section 51, as the owner or registered holder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Need the corporation inquire into a duty owed to a third person by a registered holder` IF `the corporation is not required to inquire into or see to the duty within s 51(4)` `the duty is owed to a third person` `the duty is owed by a registered holder of a security of the corporation` `the duty is owed by a person the corporation treats, as permitted or required by section 51, as the owner or registered holder`

@export May the corporation treat the surviving joint holders as the owner (s 51(6))?
GIVEN `the security was issued to persons as joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security was issued to persons as joint holders?
      `the corporation receives proof of the death of a joint holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation receives proof of the death of a joint holder?
      `the corporation is satisfied with the proof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is satisfied with the proof?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation treat the surviving joint holders as the owner` IF `the corporation may treat the survivors as owner of the security within s 51(6)` `the security was issued to persons as joint holders` `the corporation receives proof of the death of a joint holder` `the corporation is satisfied with the proof`

@export Have I deposited what the corporation may require to register a transmission on death (s 51(7))?
GIVEN `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate?
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person?
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province?
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission?
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder?
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)?
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65?
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I deposited what the corporation may require to register a transmission on death` IF `the documents required by subsection 51(7) have been deposited within s 51(7)` `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77`

@export Am I entitled to become, or to designate, a registered holder of a deceased holder's security (s 51(7))?
GIVEN `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)` @desc What is the capacity of the person?
      `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate?
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person?
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province?
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission?
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder?
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)?
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65?
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77?
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to become, or to designate, a registered holder of a deceased holder's security` IF `the person is entitled to become or designate a registered holder within s 51(7)` `the capacity of the person` `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way`

@export As a personal representative, am I entitled to become, or to designate, a registered holder without a grant of probate (s 51(8))?
GIVEN `the person is a personal representative of the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a personal representative of the deceased holder?
      `the laws governing the transmission do not require a grant of probate or letters of administration or the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the laws governing the transmission do not require a grant of probate or letters of administration or the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes?
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder?
      `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder?
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a personal representative, am I entitled to become, or to designate, a registered holder without a grant of probate` IF `the personal representative is entitled to become or designate a registered holder within s 51(8)` `the person is a personal representative of the deceased holder` `the laws governing the transmission do not require a grant of probate or letters of administration or the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes` `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way`

@export May the corporation record the transmission and treat the new registered holder as owner (s 51(9))?
GIVEN `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate?
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person?
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province?
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission?
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder?
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)?
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65?
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77?
      `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation record the transmission and treat the new registered holder as owner` IF `the corporation may record the transmission and treat the new registered holder as owner within s 51(9)` `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder`

§§ `Overissue, evidence and delivery obligations (ss 52 to 54)`

@export What may I do if validating or issuing my security would be an overissue (s 52(1))?
GIVEN `validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue?
      `a valid security similar in all respects is reasonably available for purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a valid security similar in all respects is reasonably available for purchase?
      `the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security in dollars?
GIVETH A `Outcome where validation or issue would result in overissue under s 52(1)`
DECIDE `What may I do if validating or issuing my security would be an overissue` IS `what the person entitled to validation or issue may do within s 52(1)` `validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue` `a valid security similar in all respects is reasonably available for purchase` `the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security in dollars`

@export Are the overissued securities valid from the date of issue after the articles are amended (s 52(2))?
GIVEN `the number of securities authorized after the amendment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of securities authorized after the amendment?
      `the number of securities previously authorized` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of securities previously authorized?
      `the number of securities overissued` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of securities overissued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the overissued securities valid from the date of issue after the articles are amended` IF `the overissued securities are valid from the date of their issue within s 52(2)` `the number of securities authorized after the amendment` `the number of securities previously authorized` `the number of securities overissued`

@export Is the signature on the security admitted in the action (s 53(a))?
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is an action on a security?
      `the signature is on the security or in a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is on the security or in a necessary endorsement?
      `the signature is specifically denied in the pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is specifically denied in the pleadings?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the signature on the security admitted in the action` IF `the signature is admitted within s 53(a)` `the action is an action on a security` `the signature is on the security or in a necessary endorsement` `the signature is specifically denied in the pleadings`

@export Is the signature presumed to be genuine and authorized (s 53(b))?
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is an action on a security?
      `the signature is on the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is on the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the signature presumed to be genuine and authorized` IF `the signature is presumed to be genuine and authorized within s 53(b)` `the action is an action on a security` `the signature is on the security`

@export Does producing the security entitle me to recover on it (s 53(c))?
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is an action on a security?
      `a signature is admitted or established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a signature is admitted or established?
      `the instrument is produced by a holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the instrument is produced by a holder?
      `the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does producing the security entitle me to recover on it` IF `production of the instrument entitles the holder to recover within s 53(c)` `the action is an action on a security` `a signature is admitted or established` `the instrument is produced by a holder` `the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security`

@export May I deliver any security of the specified issue where I must deliver securities (s 54)?
GIVEN `the person is required to deliver securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is required to deliver securities?
      `the security delivered is of the specified issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security delivered is of the specified issue?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `a provision of this Act, of another applicable Act, of an applicable regulation or an applicable stock exchange rule requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a provision of this Act, of another applicable Act, of an applicable regulation or an applicable stock exchange rule requires otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I deliver any security of the specified issue where I must deliver securities` IF `the person may deliver any security of the specified issue within s 54` `the person is required to deliver securities` `the security delivered is of the specified issue` `the parties otherwise agreed` `a provision of this Act, of another applicable Act, of an applicable regulation or an applicable stock exchange rule requires otherwise`

§§ `Terms of a security and defences (ss 55 to 59)`

@export Is this term a term of my security (s 55(1))?
GIVEN `the term is stated on the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the term is stated on the security?
      `the term is incorporated in the security by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the term is incorporated in the security by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order?
      `the incorporated term conflicts with a stated term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the incorporated term conflicts with a stated term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this term a term of my security` IF `the term is a term of the security within s 55(1)` `the term is stated on the security` `the term is incorporated in the security by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order` `the incorporated term conflicts with a stated term`

@export Is the security valid in my hands as a purchaser for value without notice of a defect (s 55(2))?
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a purchaser for value?
      `the person has notice of a defect going to the validity of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has notice of a defect going to the validity of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the security valid in my hands as a purchaser for value without notice of a defect` IF `the security is valid in the hands of the purchaser for value without notice within s 55(2)` `the person is a purchaser for value` `the person has notice of a defect going to the validity of the security`

@export Is the corporation's lack-of-genuineness defence a complete defence against me (s 55(3))?
GIVEN `the security is not genuine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is not genuine?
      `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is unauthorized?
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security?
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority?
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing?
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation's lack-of-genuineness defence a complete defence against me` IF `lack of genuineness is a complete defence within s 55(3)` `the security is not genuine` `the signature is unauthorized` `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`

@export Is the corporation's defence ineffective against me as a purchaser for value (s 55(4))?
GIVEN `the defence is a defence of the issuer other than lack of genuineness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defence is a defence of the issuer other than lack of genuineness?
      `the person is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a purchaser for value?
      `the person has notice of the particular defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has notice of the particular defence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation's defence ineffective against me as a purchaser for value` IF `the defence of the issuer is ineffective against the purchaser within s 55(4)` `the defence is a defence of the issuer other than lack of genuineness` `the person is a purchaser for value` `the person has notice of the particular defence`

@export Am I deemed to have notice of a defect or defence because of a call or maturity date (s 56)?
GIVEN `the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender?
      `the money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange?
      `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set? (yes or no)
      `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date set for payment or exchange? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was? (yes or no)
      `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the purchaser takes the security` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the purchaser takes the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have notice of a defect or defence because of a call or maturity date` IF `the purchaser is deemed to have notice of a defect or defence within s 56` `the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender` `the money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange` `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set as the rule reads it` `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was as the rule reads it` `the date the purchaser takes the security`
    WHERE
        `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is an unauthorized signature effective in my favour (s 57)?
GIVEN `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is unauthorized?
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security?
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority?
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing?
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an unauthorized signature effective in my favour` IF `an unauthorized signature is effective in favour of the purchaser within s 57` `the signature is unauthorized` `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`

@export Is an unauthorized signature ineffective (s 57)?
GIVEN `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is unauthorized?
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security?
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority?
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing?
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an unauthorized signature ineffective` IF `an unauthorized signature is ineffective within s 57` `the signature is unauthorized` `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`

@export May I complete a security by filling in the blanks (s 58(1))?
GIVEN `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer?
      `the security is incomplete in some other respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is incomplete in some other respect?
      `the blanks are filled in in accordance with the authority of the person completing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the blanks are filled in in accordance with the authority of the person completing it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I complete a security by filling in the blanks` IF `a person may complete the security by filling in the blanks within s 58(1)(a)` `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` `the security is incomplete in some other respect` `the blanks are filled in in accordance with the authority of the person completing it`

@export Can I enforce the security as completed (s 58(1))?
GIVEN `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer?
      `the security was incomplete in some other respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security was incomplete in some other respect?
      `the blanks were incorrectly filled in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the blanks were incorrectly filled in?
      `the person enforcing it took it for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person enforcing it took it for value?
      `the person enforcing it took it without notice of the incorrectness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person enforcing it took it without notice of the incorrectness?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I enforce the security as completed` IF `the security as completed is enforceable by the purchaser within s 58(1)(b)` `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` `the security was incomplete in some other respect` `the blanks were incorrectly filled in` `the person enforcing it took it for value` `the person enforcing it took it without notice of the incorrectness`

@export Is an altered security enforceable only on its original terms (s 58(2))?
GIVEN `the security is a completed security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is a completed security?
      `the security has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an altered security enforceable only on its original terms` IF `the security remains enforceable only according to its original terms within s 58(2)` `the security is a completed security` `the security has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently`

@export What warranties do I give as an authenticating trustee, registrar or transfer agent when I sign a security (s 59(1))?
GIVEN `the person signs the security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person signs the security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security?
      `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is a purchaser for value without notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given on signing a security under s 59(1)`)
DECIDE `What warranties do I give as an authenticating trustee, registrar or transfer agent when I sign a security` IS `the warranties the signer gives within s 59(1)` `the person signs the security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security` `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice`

@export Do I assume no further liability for the validity of the security (s 59(2))?
GIVEN `the person is one referred to in subsection 59(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one referred to in subsection 59(1)?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I assume no further liability for the validity of the security` IF `the person assumes no further liability for the validity of the security within s 59(2)` `the person is one referred to in subsection 59(1)` `the parties otherwise agreed`

§§ `Purchasers, notice and warranties on transfer (ss 60 to 64)`

@export What rights do I acquire on delivery of a security (s 60(1))?
GIVEN `the security is delivered to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is delivered to the purchaser?
      `the purchaser has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security?
      `the purchaser as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim?
      `the purchaser takes from a later bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser takes from a later bona fide purchaser?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Rights a purchaser acquires on delivery under s 60(1)`
DECIDE `What rights do I acquire on delivery of a security` IS `the rights the purchaser acquires on delivery within s 60(1)` `the security is delivered to the purchaser` `the purchaser has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security` `the purchaser as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim` `the purchaser takes from a later bona fide purchaser`

@export Do I acquire the security free from any adverse claim as a bona fide purchaser (s 60(2))?
GIVEN `the security is delivered to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is delivered to the purchaser?
      `the purchaser is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser is a bona fide purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I acquire the security free from any adverse claim as a bona fide purchaser` IF `the bona fide purchaser acquires the security free from any adverse claim within s 60(2)` `the security is delivered to the purchaser` `the purchaser is a bona fide purchaser`

@export Do I acquire the right I claim, given the interest I bought (s 60(3))?
GIVEN `the extent of the interest or right purchased` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the extent of the interest or right purchased?
      `the extent of the interest or right the purchaser claims` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the extent of the interest or right the purchaser claims?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I acquire the right I claim, given the interest I bought` IF `the purchaser acquires the right claimed within s 60(3)` `the extent of the interest or right purchased` `the extent of the interest or right the purchaser claims`

@export Am I deemed to have notice of an adverse claim because of how the security is endorsed or marked (s 61(1))?
GIVEN `the security has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for some other purpose not involving transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for some other purpose not involving transfer?
      `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is in bearer form?
      `the security has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor?
      `the statement is the mere writing of a name on the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement is the mere writing of a name on the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have notice of an adverse claim because of how the security is endorsed or marked` IF `the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim within s 61(1)` `the security has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for some other purpose not involving transfer` `the security is in bearer form` `the security has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor` `the statement is the mere writing of a name on the security`

@export Am I deemed to have notice of an adverse claim because the security is held by a fiduciary (s 61(2))?
GIVEN `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary?
      `the purchaser or broker knows that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser or broker knows that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have notice of an adverse claim because the security is held by a fiduciary` IS `the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim within s 61(2)` `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary` `the purchaser or broker knows that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's duty`

@export Must I inquire into the rightfulness of a transfer by a fiduciary (s 61(2))?
GIVEN `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I inquire into the rightfulness of a transfer by a fiduciary` IS `the purchaser or broker has a duty to inquire into the rightfulness of the transfer within s 61(2)` `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary`

@export Is an event, such as a call or a maturity, of itself notice to me of an adverse claim (s 62)?
GIVEN `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange? (yes or no)
      `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender? (yes or no)
      `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `funds are available for payment on the date set for payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that funds are available for payment on the date set for payment?
      `the date of the purchase` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the purchase?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an event, such as a call or a maturity, of itself notice to me of an adverse claim` IF `the event is of itself notice of an adverse claim within s 62` `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange as the rule reads it` `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender as the rule reads it` `funds are available for payment on the date set for payment` `the date of the purchase`
    WHERE
        `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export What warranties do I give the corporation when I present a security for registration or payment (s 63(1))?
GIVEN `the person presents the security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person presents the security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange?
      `the person is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
DECIDE `What warranties do I give the corporation when I present a security for registration or payment` IS `the warranties given to the issuer within s 63(1)` `the person presents the security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange` `the person is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer`

@export What warranties do I give a purchaser when I transfer a security to them for value (s 63(2))?
GIVEN `the person transfers the security to a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person transfers the security to a purchaser for value?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
DECIDE `What warranties do I give a purchaser when I transfer a security to them for value` IS `the warranties given to the purchaser within s 63(2)` `the person transfers the security to a purchaser for value`

@export What warranties do I give as an intermediary delivering a security (s 63(3))?
GIVEN `the security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim against the delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim against the delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
DECIDE `What warranties do I give as an intermediary delivering a security` IS `the warranties given by the intermediary within s 63(3)` `the security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim against the delivery`

@export What warranties do I give as a pledgee who redelivers a security (s 63(4))?
GIVEN `the person is a pledgee or other holder for purposes of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a pledgee or other holder for purposes of security?
      `the person redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the order of the debtor delivers it to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the order of the debtor delivers it to a third person?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
DECIDE `What warranties do I give as a pledgee who redelivers a security` IS `the warranties given by the pledgee within s 63(4)` `the person is a pledgee or other holder for purposes of security` `the person redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the order of the debtor delivers it to a third person`

@export Do I give the warranties of a purchaser as a broker (s 63(5))?
GIVEN `the person is a broker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a broker?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I give the warranties of a purchaser as a broker` IF `the broker gives the warranties and has the rights and privileges of a purchaser under this section within s 63(5)` `the person is a broker`

@export Can I be a bona fide purchaser of a registered security delivered without a necessary endorsement (s 64)?
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is in registered form?
      `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement?
      `the endorsement has been supplied by the time asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement has been supplied by the time asked about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be a bona fide purchaser of a registered security delivered without a necessary endorsement` IS `the purchaser may be a bona fide purchaser at the time asked about within s 64` `the security is in registered form` `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement` `the endorsement has been supplied by the time asked about`

@export As transferee, can I enforce the supplying of the missing endorsement (s 64)?
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is in registered form?
      `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As transferee, can I enforce the supplying of the missing endorsement` IF `against the transferor the transfer is complete on delivery and the purchaser may enforce the supplying of the endorsement within s 64` `the security is in registered form` `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement`

§§ `Endorsements and guarantees of signature (ss 65 to 69)`

@export Am I an appropriate person to endorse the security (s 65(1))?
GIVEN `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security?
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity?
      `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving?
      `the person is the successor of that fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the successor of that fiduciary?
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity?
      `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries?
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability?
      `the person is the fiduciary of that individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the fiduciary of that individual?
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign?
      `the person is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a survivor?
      `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney?
      `the principal is a person described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the principal is a person described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)?
      `the principal may act through an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the principal may act through an agent or mandatary?
      `the person is the authorized agent or mandatary of the principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the authorized agent or mandatary of the principal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an appropriate person to endorse the security` IF `the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security` `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity` `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving` `the person is the successor of that fiduciary` `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity` `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries` `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability` `the person is the fiduciary of that individual` `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign` `the person is a survivor` `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney` `the principal is a person described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)` `the principal may act through an agent or mandatary` `the person is the authorized agent or mandatary of the principal`

@export Is my endorsement authorized for the purposes of Part VII (s 65(2))?
GIVEN `the person signing was an appropriate person at the time of signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person signing was an appropriate person at the time of signing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my endorsement authorized for the purposes of Part VII` IF `the endorsement is authorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(2)` `the person signing was an appropriate person at the time of signing`

@export Is this an endorsement of a security in registered form (s 65(3))?
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is in registered form?
      `an appropriate person signs an assignment or transfer of the security, or a power to assign or transfer it, on the security or on a separate document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an appropriate person signs an assignment or transfer of the security, or a power to assign or transfer it, on the security or on a separate document?
      `the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an endorsement of a security in registered form` IF `an endorsement of a security in registered form is made within s 65(3)` `the security is in registered form` `an appropriate person signs an assignment or transfer of the security, or a power to assign or transfer it, on the security or on a separate document` `the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security`

@export What kind of endorsement is mine (s 65(4))?
GIVEN `the endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it?
      `the endorsement is to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement is to bearer?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of endorsement`
DECIDE `What kind of endorsement is mine` IS `the kind of an endorsement within s 65(4)` `the endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it` `the endorsement is to bearer`

@export May I, as holder, convert an endorsement in blank into a special endorsement (s 65(7))?
GIVEN `the person is a holder of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a holder of the security?
      `the kind of the endorsement` IS A `Kind of endorsement` @desc What is the kind of the endorsement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as holder, convert an endorsement in blank into a special endorsement` IF `a holder may convert the endorsement into a special endorsement within s 65(7)` `the person is a holder of the security` `the kind of the endorsement`

@export Do I assume any obligation that the issuer will honour the security by endorsing it (s 65(8))?
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I assume any obligation that the issuer will honour the security by endorsing it` IF `the endorser assumes no obligation that the security will be honoured by the issuer within s 65(8)` `the parties otherwise agreed`

@export For how many units is my endorsement effective (s 65(9))?
GIVEN `the endorsement purports to be only of part of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement purports to be only of part of a security?
      `the security represents units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security represents units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable?
      `the number of units the endorsement covers` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of units the endorsement covers?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many units is my endorsement effective` IS `the number of units for which the endorsement is effective within s 65(9)` `the endorsement purports to be only of part of a security` `the security represents units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable` `the number of units the endorsement covers`

@export Does a failure make my endorsement as a fiduciary unauthorized (s 65(10))?
GIVEN `the fiduciary failed to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law governing the fiduciary relationship, including a law requiring court approval of a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fiduciary failed to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law governing the fiduciary relationship, including a law requiring court approval of a transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a failure make my endorsement as a fiduciary unauthorized` IS `the failure makes the fiduciary's endorsement unauthorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(10)` `the fiduciary failed to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law governing the fiduciary relationship, including a law requiring court approval of a transfer`

@export Does my endorsement constitute a transfer (s 66)?
GIVEN `the security on which the endorsement appears has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security on which the endorsement appears has been delivered?
      `the endorsement is on a separate document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement is on a separate document?
      `the separate document has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the separate document has been delivered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my endorsement constitute a transfer` IF `the endorsement constitutes a transfer within s 66` `the security on which the endorsement appears has been delivered` `the endorsement is on a separate document` `the separate document has been delivered`

@export May an endorsement give notice of an adverse claim (s 67)?
GIVEN `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is in bearer form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an endorsement give notice of an adverse claim` IF `an endorsement of the security may give notice of an adverse claim under section 61 within s 67` `the security is in bearer form`

@export May I, as owner, assert that the endorsement was ineffective against the other party (s 68(1))?
GIVEN `the endorsement is unauthorized or otherwise ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement is unauthorized or otherwise ineffective?
      `the other party is the issuer or a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is the issuer or a purchaser?
      `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer?
      `the owner has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security?
      `the owner is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as owner, assert that the endorsement was ineffective against the other party` IF `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the endorsement against the other party within s 68(1)` `the endorsement is unauthorized or otherwise ineffective` `the other party is the issuer or a purchaser` `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer` `the owner has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security` `the owner is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement`

@export Is the corporation liable to me for improper registration (s 68(2))?
GIVEN `the issuer registered the transfer of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registered the transfer of the security?
      `the registration was made on an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registration was made on an unauthorized endorsement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation liable to me for improper registration` IF `the issuer is liable for improper registration within s 68(2)` `the issuer registered the transfer of the security` `the registration was made on an unauthorized endorsement`

@export What do I warrant when I guarantee a signature (s 69(1))?
GIVEN `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty of a guarantor under s 69`)
DECIDE `What do I warrant when I guarantee a signature` IS `the warranties a guarantor of a signature gives within s 69(1)` `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security`

@export Do I warrant that a particular transfer is rightful when I guarantee a signature (s 69(2))?
GIVEN `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I warrant that a particular transfer is rightful when I guarantee a signature` IS `a guarantor of a signature warrants the rightfulness of the particular transfer within s 69(2)` `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security`

@export What do I warrant when I guarantee an endorsement (s 69(3))?
GIVEN `the person guarantees an endorsement of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person guarantees an endorsement of a security?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty of a guarantor under s 69`)
DECIDE `What do I warrant when I guarantee an endorsement` IS `the warranties a guarantor of an endorsement gives within s 69(3)` `the person guarantees an endorsement of a security`

@export May the corporation require a guarantee of an endorsement (s 69(3))?
GIVEN `the issuer requires a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer requires a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation require a guarantee of an endorsement` IS `the issuer's requirement of a guarantee of endorsement is permitted within s 69(3)` `the issuer requires a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer`

@export Are a guarantor's warranties made to me (s 69(4))?
GIVEN `the person takes or deals with the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person takes or deals with the security?
      `the person relies on the guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person relies on the guarantee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are a guarantor's warranties made to me` IF `the warranties are made to the person within s 69(4)` `the person takes or deals with the security` `the person relies on the guarantee`

@export How much is a guarantor liable to me for (s 69(4))?
GIVEN `the person takes or deals with the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person takes or deals with the security?
      `the person relies on the guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person relies on the guarantee?
      `a warranty referred to in section 69 was breached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a warranty referred to in section 69 was breached?
      `the loss resulting from the breach in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the loss resulting from the breach in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is a guarantor liable to me for` IS `the guarantor's liability to the person in dollars within s 69(4)` `the person takes or deals with the security` `the person relies on the guarantee` `a warranty referred to in section 69 was breached` `the loss resulting from the breach in dollars`

§§ `Delivery, reclaiming and rejecting securities (ss 70 to 75)`

@export Does delivery to me occur through my broker (s 70(1))?
GIVEN `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser?
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does delivery to me occur through my broker` IF `delivery occurs through the purchaser's broker within s 70(1)` `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser`

@export Does delivery to me occur (s 70(1))?
GIVEN `the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security?
      `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser?
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser?
      `a third person in possession of an identified security to be delivered acknowledges holding it for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a third person in possession of an identified security to be delivered acknowledges holding it for the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does delivery to me occur` IF `delivery to a purchaser occurs within s 70(1)` `the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security` `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` `a third person in possession of an identified security to be delivered acknowledges holding it for the purchaser`

@export Am I the owner of a security my broker holds for me (s 70(2))?
GIVEN `a broker holds the security for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a broker holds the security for the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the owner of a security my broker holds for me` IF `the purchaser is the owner of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser within s 70(2)` `a broker holds the security for the purchaser`

@export Am I a holder of a security my broker holds for me (s 70(2))?
GIVEN `a broker holds the security for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a broker holds the security for the purchaser?
      `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser?
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a holder of a security my broker holds for me` IF `the purchaser is a holder of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser within s 70(2)` `a broker holds the security for the purchaser` `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser`

@export What is my proportionate share of the fungible bulk my broker holds (s 70(3))?
GIVEN `the security is part of a fungible bulk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is part of a fungible bulk?
      `the number of securities the purchaser purchased` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of securities the purchaser purchased?
      `the number of securities in the fungible bulk` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of securities in the fungible bulk?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my proportionate share of the fungible bulk my broker holds` IS `the purchaser's proportionate share of the fungible bulk within s 70(3)` `the security is part of a fungible bulk` `the number of securities the purchaser purchased` `the number of securities in the fungible bulk`

@export Is notice of an adverse claim ineffective against my broker and me (s 70(4))?
GIVEN `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is notice of an adverse claim ineffective against my broker and me` IF `the notice of an adverse claim is ineffective against the broker and the purchaser within s 70(4)` `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value`

@export May I demand delivery of an equivalent security from my broker (s 70(4))?
GIVEN `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I demand delivery of an equivalent security from my broker` IF `the purchaser may demand delivery of an equivalent security from the broker within s 70(4)` `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value`

@export Have I, as the selling customer, fulfilled my duty to deliver (s 71(1))?
GIVEN `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `the selling customer delivers the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the selling customer delivers the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker?
      `the selling customer causes an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that the security is held for the selling broker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the selling customer causes an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that the security is held for the selling broker?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I, as the selling customer, fulfilled my duty to deliver` IF `the selling customer has fulfilled the duty to deliver within s 71(1)` `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` `the parties otherwise agreed` `the selling customer delivers the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker` `the selling customer causes an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that the security is held for the selling broker`

@export Has my selling broker fulfilled the duty to deliver (s 71(1))?
GIVEN `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `the selling broker delivers the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the selling broker delivers the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker?
      `the selling broker effects clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the selling broker effects clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my selling broker fulfilled the duty to deliver` IF `the selling broker has fulfilled the duty to deliver within s 71(1)` `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` `the parties otherwise agreed` `the selling broker delivers the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker` `the selling broker effects clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place`

@export Have I, as transferor, fulfilled my duty to deliver under a contract of purchase (s 71(2))?
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser?
      `the transferor causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transferor causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I, as transferor, fulfilled my duty to deliver under a contract of purchase` IF `the transferor has fulfilled the duty to deliver under a contract of purchase within s 71(2)` `the parties otherwise agreed` `the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser` `the transferor causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser`

@export Does the contract-of-purchase rule govern this sale rather than the broker rule (s 71(3))?
GIVEN `the sale is to a broker purchasing for the broker's own account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sale is to a broker purchasing for the broker's own account?
      `the sale is made on a stock exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sale is made on a stock exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the contract-of-purchase rule govern this sale rather than the broker rule` IF `subsection 71(2) governs the sale and subsection 71(1) does not within s 71(3)` `the sale is to a broker purchasing for the broker's own account` `the sale is made on a stock exchange`

@export May I reclaim possession of the security, obtain a new one or claim damages (s 72(1))?
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity?
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is a bona fide purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I reclaim possession of the security, obtain a new one or claim damages` IF `the person may reclaim possession, obtain a new security or claim damages within s 72(1)` `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` `the other party is a bona fide purchaser`

@export May I, as owner, reclaim possession even from a bona fide purchaser (s 72(2))?
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement?
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as owner, reclaim possession even from a bona fide purchaser` IF `the owner may reclaim possession even from a bona fide purchaser within s 72(2)` `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

@export Do I have a right to reclaim possession of the security (s 72)?
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity?
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is a bona fide purchaser?
      `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement?
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a right to reclaim possession of the security` IF `the person has a right to reclaim possession of the security within s 72(2)` `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

@export May my right to reclaim possession be specifically enforced and the security impounded (s 72(3))?
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity?
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other party is a bona fide purchaser?
      `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement?
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my right to reclaim possession be specifically enforced and the security impounded` IF `the right to reclaim possession may be specifically enforced, the transfer restrained and the security impounded or sequestrated pending litigation within s 72(3)` `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

@export Must the transferor supply the proof or requisite I need to register the transfer (s 73(1))?
GIVEN `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `the transfer is for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is for value?
      `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the transferor supply the proof or requisite I need to register the transfer` IF `the transferor must supply the proof or requisite within s 73(1)` `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` `the parties otherwise agreed` `the transfer is for value` `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer`

@export May I reject or rescind the transfer (s 73(2))?
GIVEN `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer?
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agreed?
      `the transfer is for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is for value?
      `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer?
      `the transferor fails to comply with the demand within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transferor fails to comply with the demand within a reasonable time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I reject or rescind the transfer` IF `the purchaser may reject or rescind the transfer within s 73(2)` `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` `the parties otherwise agreed` `the transfer is for value` `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer` `the transferor fails to comply with the demand within a reasonable time`

@export Is a seizure of my security ineffective (s 74)?
GIVEN `the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a seizure of my security ineffective` IF `the seizure is ineffective within s 74` `the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security`

@export Am I protected from liability for conversion or for taking part in a breach of fiduciary duty (s 75)?
GIVEN `the person is an agent, mandatary or bailee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an agent, mandatary or bailee?
      `the person has received securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has received securities?
      `the person sold, pledged or delivered them according to the instructions of their principal or mandator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person sold, pledged or delivered them according to the instructions of their principal or mandator?
      `the person acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acted in good faith?
      `the person is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation?
      `the person observed reasonable commercial standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person observed reasonable commercial standards?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from liability for conversion or for taking part in a breach of fiduciary duty` IF `the person is not liable for conversion or for participation in breach of fiduciary duty within s 75` `the person is an agent, mandatary or bailee` `the person has received securities` `the person sold, pledged or delivered them according to the instructions of their principal or mandator` `the person acted in good faith` `the person is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation` `the person observed reasonable commercial standards`

§§ `Registration of a transfer (ss 76 to 81)`

@export Must the corporation register my transfer (s 76(1))?
GIVEN `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a security in registered form is presented for transfer?
      `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65?
      `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective?
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with?
      `the transfer is rightful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is rightful?
      `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser?
      `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation register my transfer` IF `the issuer must register the transfer within s 76(1)` `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` `the transfer is rightful` `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid`

@export How much is the corporation liable to me for if it does not register my transfer (s 76(2))?
GIVEN `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a security in registered form is presented for transfer?
      `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65?
      `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective?
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with?
      `the transfer is rightful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is rightful?
      `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser?
      `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid?
      `the issuer unreasonably delays the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer unreasonably delays the registration?
      `the issuer fails or refuses to register the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer fails or refuses to register the transfer?
      `the loss resulting from the delay, failure or refusal in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the loss resulting from the delay, failure or refusal in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the corporation liable to me for if it does not register my transfer` IS `the issuer's liability to the person presenting the security in dollars within s 76(2)` `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` `the transfer is rightful` `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid` `the issuer unreasonably delays the registration` `the issuer fails or refuses to register the transfer` `the loss resulting from the delay, failure or refusal in dollars`

@export What may the corporation require of me before it registers my transfer (s 77(1))?
GIVEN `the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary?
      `the endorsement is by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement is by a fiduciary?
      `there is more than one fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is more than one fiduciary?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Requirement an issuer may make under s 77(1)`
DECIDE `What may the corporation require of me before it registers my transfer` IS `what the issuer may require within s 77(1)` `the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary` `the endorsement is by a fiduciary` `there is more than one fiduciary`

@export Is the guarantee of the signature that the corporation requires satisfied (s 77(2))?
GIVEN `the guarantee is signed by or on behalf of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the guarantee is signed by or on behalf of a person?
      `the issuer reasonably believes that person to be responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer reasonably believes that person to be responsible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the guarantee of the signature that the corporation requires satisfied` IF `guarantee of the signature within s 77(2)` `the guarantee is signed by or on behalf of a person` `the issuer reasonably believes that person to be responsible`

@export May the corporation adopt standards to decide who is a responsible person (s 77(3))?
GIVEN `the standards are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the standards are reasonable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation adopt standards to decide who is a responsible person` IF `the issuer may adopt the standards to determine responsible persons within s 77(3)` `the standards are reasonable`

@export Is my evidence of appointment or incumbency sufficient (s 77(4))?
GIVEN `the fiduciary was appointed by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fiduciary was appointed by a court?
      `the document is a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)?
      `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the order?
      `the date the security is presented for transfer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the security is presented for transfer?
      `the document is a copy of a document showing the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is a copy of a document showing the appointment?
      `the document is other evidence the issuer believes to be appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is other evidence the issuer believes to be appropriate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my evidence of appointment or incumbency sufficient` IF `evidence of appointment or incumbency within s 77(4)` `the fiduciary was appointed by a court` `the document is a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)` `the date of the order` `the date the security is presented for transfer` `the document is a copy of a document showing the appointment` `the document is other evidence the issuer believes to be appropriate`

@export May the corporation adopt standards for the evidence of appointment (s 77(5))?
GIVEN `the standards are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the standards are reasonable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation adopt standards for the evidence of appointment` IF `the issuer may adopt the standards for evidence under paragraph 77(4)(b) within s 77(5)` `the standards are reasonable`

@export Does the corporation have notice of the contents of the document I furnish (s 77(6))?
GIVEN `the document is a document referred to in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is a document referred to in subsection 77(4)?
      `the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation have notice of the contents of the document I furnish` IS `the issuer has notice of the contents within s 77(6)` `the document is a document referred to in subsection 77(4)` `the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency`

@export Is the corporation deemed to have notice of all matters in the document that affect the transfer (s 77(7))?
GIVEN `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)?
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation deemed to have notice of all matters in the document that affect the transfer` IF `the issuer is deemed to have notice of all matters contained in the document affecting the transfer within s 77(7)` `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document`

@export Has the corporation a duty to inquire into an adverse claim before registering the transfer (s 78(1))?
GIVEN `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security?
      `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part?
      `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was received?
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was last renewed in writing? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
      `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)?
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document?
      `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation a duty to inquire into an adverse claim before registering the transfer` IF `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims within s 78(1)` `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` `the date the written notice was received` `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` `the day asked about` `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim`
    WHERE
        `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has the corporation discharged its duty of inquiry into an adverse claim (s 78(2))?
GIVEN `the issuer used another reasonable means to discharge the duty of inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer used another reasonable means to discharge the duty of inquiry?
      `the issuer notified the adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer notified the adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business?
      `the notice stated that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court or is provided with a sufficient indemnity bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice stated that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court or is provided with a sufficient indemnity bond?
      `the date of mailing` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of mailing?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
      `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation discharged its duty of inquiry into an adverse claim` IF `the issuer has discharged the duty of inquiry within s 78(2)` `the issuer used another reasonable means to discharge the duty of inquiry` `the issuer notified the adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business` `the notice stated that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court or is provided with a sufficient indemnity bond` `the date of mailing` `the day asked about` `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was as the rule reads it` `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Had the corporation no duty to inquire, or has it discharged it (s 78(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Had the corporation no duty to inquire, or has it discharged it (s 78(1) and (2))` IF `the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty within s 78(1)` `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`

@export Has the corporation no duty to inquire into an adverse claim (s 78(3))?
GIVEN `the security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65?
      `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security?
      `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part?
      `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was received?
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was last renewed in writing? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
      `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)?
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document?
      `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation no duty to inquire into an adverse claim` IF `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims within s 78(3)` `the security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65` `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` `the date the written notice was received` `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` `the day asked about` `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim`
    WHERE
        `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my written notice of adverse claim effective against the corporation (s 78(4))?
GIVEN `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was received?
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written notice was last renewed in writing? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my written notice of adverse claim effective against the corporation` IF `the written notice of adverse claim is effective within s 78(4)` `the date the written notice was received` `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the corporation bound to inquire into the fiduciary relationship (s 78(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)?
      `the issuer registers the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registers the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation bound to inquire into the fiduciary relationship (s 78(3)(a))` IS `the issuer is bound to inquire into the existence, extent or correct description of the fiduciary relationship within s 78(3)(a)` `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` `the issuer registers the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary`

@export May the corporation assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary (s 78(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)?
      `the issuer registered the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registered the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary?
      `the issuer has received written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has received written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary (s 78(3)(a))` IF `the issuer may assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary within s 78(3)(a)` `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` `the issuer registered the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary` `the issuer has received written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security`

@export Has the corporation no duty to inquire whether the transfer complies with the document or governing law (s 78(3)(b))?
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)?
      `the issuer registers the transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registers the transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation no duty to inquire whether the transfer complies with the document or governing law (s 78(3)(b))` IF `the issuer has no duty to inquire whether the transfer complies with the document or the governing law within s 78(3)(b)` `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` `the issuer registers the transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary`

@export Is the corporation deemed not to have notice of the contents of the record or document (s 78(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)?
      `the document is a court record or a registered document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is a court record or a registered document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation deemed not to have notice of the contents of the record or document (s 78(3)(c))` IF `the issuer is deemed not to have notice of the contents of the record or document within s 78(3)(c)` `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` `the document is a court record or a registered document`

@export Is the corporation not liable for loss resulting from registering a transfer (s 79(1))?
GIVEN `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the necessary endorsements were on or with the security?
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation not liable for loss resulting from registering a transfer` IF `the issuer is not liable for loss resulting from the registration within s 79(1)` `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable`

@export Must the corporation deliver a like security to me as owner on demand (s 79(2))?
GIVEN `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it?
      `the owner demands delivery of a like security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner demands delivery of a like security?
      `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the necessary endorsements were on or with the security?
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims?
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable?
      `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken?
      `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking?
      `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice?
      `the delivery would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the delivery would result in overissue?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation deliver a like security to me as owner on demand` IF `the issuer must deliver a like security to the owner on demand within s 79(2)` `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` `the owner demands delivery of a like security` `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable` `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice` `the delivery would result in overissue`

@export Is the corporation's liability for the like security governed by s 52 (s 79(2))?
GIVEN `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it?
      `the owner demands delivery of a like security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner demands delivery of a like security?
      `the delivery would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the delivery would result in overissue?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation's liability for the like security governed by s 52` IF `the issuer's liability is governed by section 52 within s 79(2)` `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` `the owner demands delivery of a like security` `the delivery would result in overissue`

@export Am I precluded from asserting a claim to a new security against the corporation (s 80(1))?
GIVEN `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken?
      `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking?
      `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I precluded from asserting a claim to a new security against the corporation` IF `the owner is precluded from asserting against the issuer any claim to a new security within s 80(1)` `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice`

@export Must the corporation issue me a new security in place of the original (s 80(2))?
GIVEN `the owner claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken?
      `the owner requests a new security before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner requests a new security before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser?
      `the owner furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond?
      `the owner satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the owner satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation issue me a new security in place of the original` IF `the issuer must issue a new security in place of the original within s 80(2)` `the owner claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken` `the owner requests a new security before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser` `the owner furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond` `the owner satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer`

@export Must the corporation register the transfer I present as a bona fide purchaser of the original (s 80(3))?
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)?
      `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer?
      `registration would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that registration would result in overissue?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation register the transfer I present as a bona fide purchaser of the original` IF `the issuer must register the transfer presented by the bona fide purchaser of the original within s 80(3)` `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` `registration would result in overissue`

@export Is the corporation's liability on the original governed by s 52 (s 80(3))?
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)?
      `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer?
      `registration would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that registration would result in overissue?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation's liability on the original governed by s 52` IF `the issuer's liability is governed by section 52 within s 80(3)` `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` `registration would result in overissue`

@export May the corporation recover the new security from the party who received it (s 80(4))?
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)?
      `the party is the person to whom the new security was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the party is the person to whom the new security was issued?
      `the party takes under the person to whom the new security was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the party takes under the person to whom the new security was issued?
      `the party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the party is a bona fide purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation recover the new security from the party who received it` IF `the issuer may recover the new security from the party within s 80(4)` `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` `the party is the person to whom the new security was issued` `the party takes under the person to whom the new security was issued` `the party is a bona fide purchaser`

@export As the corporation's agent, do I owe it a duty of good faith and reasonable diligence (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer?
      `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the corporation's agent, do I owe it a duty of good faith and reasonable diligence` IF `the agent owes the issuer a duty to exercise good faith and reasonable diligence within s 81(1)` `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer`

@export As the corporation's agent, do I have the obligations, rights, privileges and immunities of the corporation (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer?
      `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the corporation's agent, do I have the obligations, rights, privileges and immunities of the corporation` IF `the agent has the same obligations, rights, privileges and immunities as the issuer within s 81(1)` `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer`

@export Is notice to the corporation's agent notice to the corporation (s 81(2))?
GIVEN `the notice is given to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is given to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer?
      `the notice relates to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice relates to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is notice to the corporation's agent notice to the corporation` IF `notice to the agent or mandatary is notice to the issuer within s 81(2)` `the notice is given to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` `the notice relates to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary`


§ `Trust indentures (Part VIII, ss 82 to 93)`

§§ `Does Part VIII apply, and who may be the trustee (ss 82 to 84)`

@export Does Part VIII apply to our trust indenture (s 82(2))?
GIVEN `the instrument is a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the instrument is a trust indenture?
      `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part VIII apply to our trust indenture` IF `this Part applies to the trust indenture within s 82(2)` `the instrument is a trust indenture` `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public`

@export May the Director exempt our trust indenture from Part VIII (s 82(3))?
GIVEN `the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director exempt our trust indenture from Part VIII` IF `the Director may exempt the trust indenture from this Part within s 82(3)` `the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part`

@export Does Part VIII apply to our trust indenture after any exemption (s 82(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the instrument is a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the instrument is a trust indenture?
      `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public?
      `the Director has exempted the trust indenture from this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Director has exempted the trust indenture from this Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part VIII apply to our trust indenture after any exemption (s 82(2) and (3))` IF `this Part applies to the trust indenture after any exemption within s 82(3)` `the instrument is a trust indenture` `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public` `the Director has exempted the trust indenture from this Part`

@export Must this person not be appointed trustee because of a conflict (s 83(1))?
GIVEN `there is a material conflict of interest between the person's role as trustee and their role in any other capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a material conflict of interest between the person's role as trustee and their role in any other capacity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this person not be appointed trustee because of a conflict` IF `the person must not be appointed as trustee within s 83(1)` `there is a material conflict of interest between the person's role as trustee and their role in any other capacity`

@export Has our trustee eliminated the conflict or resigned as required (s 83(2))?
GIVEN `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists?
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did? (yes or no)
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did? (yes or no)
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee resigned from office? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our trustee eliminated the conflict or resigned as required` IF `the trustee has complied with the duty to eliminate the conflict or resign within s 83(2)` `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did as the rule reads it` `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does the conflict invalidate the trust indenture, the debt obligations or the security interest (s 83(3))?
GIVEN `the trustee has a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee has a material conflict of interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conflict invalidate the trust indenture, the debt obligations or the security interest` IS `the conflict invalidates the trust indenture, the debt obligations or the security interest within s 83(3)` `the trustee has a material conflict of interest`

@export May I, as an interested person, apply to a court to have the trustee replaced (s 83(4))?
GIVEN `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest?
      `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists?
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did? (yes or no)
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did? (yes or no)
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee resigned from office? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is an interested person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as an interested person, apply to a court to have the trustee replaced` IF `an interested person may apply to a court for an order that the trustee be replaced within s 83(4)` `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest` `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did as the rule reads it` `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did as the rule reads it` `the day asked about` `the applicant is an interested person`
    WHERE
        `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is our trustee qualified (s 84)?
GIVEN `at least one of the trustees appointed is a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at least one of the trustees appointed is a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our trustee qualified` IF `the requirement for a qualified trustee is met within s 84` `at least one of the trustees appointed is a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company`

§§ `What the corporation must furnish the trustee (ss 85 to 89)`

@export Must our corporation furnish the trustee with the information it needs for the list of holders (s 85(2))?
GIVEN `the trustee demands information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee demands information?
      `the information is required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection 85(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection 85(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation furnish the trustee with the information it needs for the list of holders` IF `the issuer must furnish the trustee with the information within s 85(2)` `the trustee demands information` `the information is required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection 85(1)`

@export Must the trustee furnish the list of holders to a person who asks (s 85(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture?
      `the holder pays the trustee a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder pays the trustee a reasonable fee?
      `the holder delivers a statutory declaration to the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder delivers a statutory declaration to the trustee?
      `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list?
      `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person requiring the list is a body corporate?
      `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate?
      `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)?
      `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the trustee furnish the list of holders to a person who asks` IF `the trustee must furnish the list within s 85(1)` `the person is a holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture` `the holder pays the trustee a reasonable fee` `the holder delivers a statutory declaration to the trustee` `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list` `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate` `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)` `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate`

@export By what day must the trustee furnish the list (s 85(1))?
GIVEN `the date the holder delivers the statutory declaration to the trustee` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the holder delivers the statutory declaration to the trustee?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the trustee furnish the list` IS `the last day for the trustee to furnish the list within s 85(1)` `the date the holder delivers the statutory declaration to the trustee`

@export Is the statutory declaration made by the right person (s 85(3))?
GIVEN `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person requiring the list is a body corporate?
      `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the statutory declaration made by the right person` IF `the statutory declaration is made by the right person within s 85(3)` `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate`

@export Is my use of the list of holders permitted (s 85(5))?
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the list was obtained under section 85?
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my use of the list of holders permitted` IS `the use of the list is permitted within s 85(5)` `the list was obtained under section 85` `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof`

@export Am I guilty of an offence for misusing the list of holders (s 85(6))?
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the list was obtained under section 85?
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof?
      `the person acted without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acted without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for misusing the list of holders` IF `the person is guilty of an offence within s 85(6)` `the list was obtained under section 85` `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` `the person acted without reasonable cause`

@export What is the most I may be liable to on summary conviction for misusing the list (s 85(6))?
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the list was obtained under section 85?
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations?
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof?
      `the person acted without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acted without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty on summary conviction`
DECIDE `What is the most I may be liable to on summary conviction for misusing the list` IS `the most the person is liable to on summary conviction within s 85(6)` `the list was obtained under section 85` `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` `the person acted without reasonable cause`

@export Must our corporation furnish evidence of compliance before we do this act (s 86(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of act` IS A `Kind of act under s 86(1)` @desc What is the kind of act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation furnish evidence of compliance before we do this act` IF `the issuer or guarantor must furnish evidence of compliance before the act within s 86(1)` `the kind of act`

@export Must our corporation furnish evidence of compliance on the trustee's demand (s 86(2))?
GIVEN `the trustee demands evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee demands evidence?
      `the evidence is of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of an act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the evidence is of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of an act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation furnish evidence of compliance on the trustee's demand` IF `the issuer or guarantor must furnish the evidence on demand within s 86(2)` `the trustee demands evidence` `the evidence is of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of an act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor`

@export Does our evidence of compliance consist of what it must (s 87)?
GIVEN `a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor states that the conditions referred to in section 86 have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor states that the conditions referred to in section 86 have been complied with?
      `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by legal counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by legal counsel?
      `an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with is furnished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with is furnished?
      `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by an auditor or accountant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by an auditor or accountant?
      `an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or of such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with is furnished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or of such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with is furnished?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our evidence of compliance consist of what it must` IF `the evidence of compliance consists of what it must within s 87` `a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor states that the conditions referred to in section 86 have been complied with` `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by legal counsel` `an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with is furnished` `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by an auditor or accountant` `an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or of such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with is furnished`

@export Does our evidence of compliance include the statement it must (s 88)?
GIVEN `the statement declares that the person has read and understands the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement declares that the person has read and understands the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86?
      `the statement describes the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement describes the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based?
      `the statement declares that the person has made the examination or investigation they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement declares that the person has made the examination or investigation they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our evidence of compliance include the statement it must` IF `the evidence of compliance includes the statement it must within s 88` `the statement declares that the person has read and understands the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86` `the statement describes the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based` `the statement declares that the person has made the examination or investigation they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions`

@export Must our corporation furnish evidence in the form the trustee requires (s 89(1))?
GIVEN `the trustee demands evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee demands evidence?
      `the evidence is as to compliance with a condition relating to an action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the evidence is as to compliance with a condition relating to an action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation furnish evidence in the form the trustee requires` IF `the issuer or guarantor must furnish evidence in the form the trustee may require within s 89(1)` `the trustee demands evidence` `the evidence is as to compliance with a condition relating to an action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture`

@export Did we furnish a certificate in each completed twelve-month period (s 89(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the trust indenture` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the trust indenture?
      `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (first)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate
      `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (second)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate
      `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (third)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did we furnish a certificate in each completed twelve-month period` IF `a certificate was furnished in each completed twelve month period within s 89(2)` `the date of the trust indenture` `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate as a list` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate as a list` MEANS LIST `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (first)`, `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (second)`, `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate (third)`

@export Must our corporation furnish the certificate on the trustee's demand (s 89(2))?
GIVEN `the trustee demands a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee demands a certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation furnish the certificate on the trustee's demand` IF `the issuer or guarantor must furnish the certificate on demand within s 89(2)` `the trustee demands a certificate`

@export Does our certificate say what it must (s 89(2))?
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with a requirement of the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would with notice, lapse of time or otherwise constitute an event of default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been a failure to comply with a requirement of the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would with notice, lapse of time or otherwise constitute an event of default?
      `the certificate states that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all such requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all such requirements?
      `the certificate gives particulars of the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate gives particulars of the failure?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our certificate say what it must` IF `the certificate says what it must within s 89(2)` `there has been a failure to comply with a requirement of the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would with notice, lapse of time or otherwise constitute an event of default` `the certificate states that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all such requirements` `the certificate gives particulars of the failure`

§§ `The trustee's duties (ss 90 to 93)`

@export Must the trustee give the holders notice of the event of default (s 90)?
GIVEN `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture?
      `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given?
      `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice?
      `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the trustee give the holders notice of the event of default` IF `the trustee must give the holders notice of the event of default within s 90` `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice`

@export By what day must the trustee give notice of the default (s 90)?
GIVEN `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the trustee give notice of the default` IS `the last day for the trustee to give notice within s 90` `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default`

@export Is the trustee in breach of the duty to give notice of the default (s 90)?
GIVEN `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture?
      `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given?
      `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice?
      `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice?
      `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default?
      `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did? (yes or no)
      `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the trustee gave notice to the holders? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the trustee in breach of the duty to give notice of the default` IF `the trustee is in breach of the duty to give notice of default within s 90` `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice` `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has the trustee discharged the duty of care (s 91)?
GIVEN `the trustee acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture?
      `the trustee exercises the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee exercises the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the trustee discharged the duty of care` IF `the trustee has discharged the duty of care within s 91` `the trustee acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture` `the trustee exercises the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee`

@export Is the trustee not liable (s 92)?
GIVEN `the trustee relies in good faith on statements contained in a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trustee relies in good faith on statements contained in a document?
      `the document is a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report?
      `the document complies with this Act or the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document complies with this Act or the trust indenture?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the trustee not liable` IF `the trustee is not liable within s 92` `the trustee relies in good faith on statements contained in a document` `the document is a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report` `the document complies with this Act or the trust indenture`

@export Does a term of the trust indenture relieve the trustee from the duties in s 91 (s 93)?
GIVEN `the term is a term of a trust indenture, of an agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued under it, or of an agreement between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the term is a term of a trust indenture, of an agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued under it, or of an agreement between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor?
      `the term would relieve the trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the term would relieve the trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a term of the trust indenture relieve the trustee from the duties in s 91` IS `the term operates to relieve the trustee from the duties imposed by section 91 within s 93` `the term is a term of a trust indenture, of an agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued under it, or of an agreement between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor` `the term would relieve the trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91`


§ `Receivers, receiver-managers and sequestrators (Part IX, ss 94 to 101)`

§§ `What the appointee may do, and what it means for the directors (ss 94 to 100)`

@export May the receiver or sequestrator receive the income, pay the liabilities and realize the security interest (s 94)?
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX` @desc What is the kind of appointee?
      `the exercise would defeat the rights of a secured creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the exercise would defeat the rights of a secured creditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the receiver or sequestrator receive the income, pay the liabilities and realize the security interest` IF `the appointee may receive the income, pay the liabilities and realize the security interest within s 94` `the kind of appointee` `the exercise would defeat the rights of a secured creditor`

@export May the appointee carry on the business of the corporation (s 94)?
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX` @desc What is the kind of appointee?
      `a court permits the appointee to carry on the business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a court permits the appointee to carry on the business of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the appointee carry on the business of the corporation` IS `the appointee may carry on the business of the corporation within s 94` `the kind of appointee` `a court permits the appointee to carry on the business of the corporation`

@export May the receiver-manager carry on the business of the corporation (s 95)?
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX` @desc What is the kind of appointee?
      `the business is carried on to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the business is carried on to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the receiver-manager carry on the business of the corporation` IF `the receiver-manager may carry on the business of the corporation within s 95` `the kind of appointee` `the business is carried on to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed`

@export Are the directors barred from exercising a power now that a receiver has been appointed (s 96)?
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX` @desc What is the kind of appointee?
      `the appointee is authorized to exercise the power of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee is authorized to exercise the power of the directors?
      `the appointee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has been discharged?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the directors barred from exercising a power now that a receiver has been appointed` IF `the directors may not exercise the power within s 96` `the kind of appointee` `the appointee is authorized to exercise the power of the directors` `the appointee has been discharged`

@export Must the appointee act in accordance with the court's directions (s 97)?
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX` @desc What is the way the appointee is appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the appointee act in accordance with the court's directions` IF `the appointee must act in accordance with the directions of the court within s 97` `the way the appointee is appointed`

@export Must the appointee act in accordance with the instrument or act and any court direction (s 98)?
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX` @desc What is the way the appointee is appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the appointee act in accordance with the instrument or act and any court direction` IF `the appointee must act in accordance with the instrument or act and any direction of a court within s 98` `the way the appointee is appointed`

@export Has the appointee discharged the duty of care to the corporation's creditors and others (s 99)?
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX` @desc What is the way the appointee is appointed?
      `the appointee acts honestly and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee acts honestly and in good faith?
      `the appointee deals with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee deals with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee discharged the duty of care to the corporation's creditors and others` IS `the appointee has discharged the duty of care within s 99` `the way the appointee is appointed` `the appointee acts honestly and in good faith` `the appointee deals with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner`

@export May a court make any order it thinks fit about the appointee (s 100)?
GIVEN `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed?
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is an interested person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a court make any order it thinks fit about the appointee` IF `a court may make any order it thinks fit within s 100` `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` `the applicant is an interested person`

@export Which orders does the text name that a court may make about the appointee (s 100)?
GIVEN `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed?
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is an interested person?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 100`)
DECIDE `Which orders does the text name that a court may make about the appointee` IS `the orders the text names within s 100` `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` `the applicant is an interested person`

§§ `What the appointee must do for the corporation (s 101)`

@export May I, as a director, inspect the accounts of the receiver's administration (s 101(e))?
GIVEN `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director of the corporation?
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is during usual business hours?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a director, inspect the accounts of the receiver's administration` IF `a director may inspect the accounts of the administration within s 101(e)` `the person is a director of the corporation` `it is during usual business hours`

@export Has the appointee notified the Director of their appointment and discharge (s 101(a))?
GIVEN `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee notified the Director immediately of their appointment?
      `the appointee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has been discharged?
      `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee notified the Director immediately of their discharge?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee notified the Director of their appointment and discharge` IF `the appointee has notified the Director as required within s 101(a)` `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their appointment` `the appointee has been discharged` `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their discharge`

@export Has the appointee taken custody and control of the corporation's property (s 101(b))?
GIVEN `the appointee has taken the property of the corporation into their custody and control in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has taken the property of the corporation into their custody and control in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee taken custody and control of the corporation's property` IF `the appointee has taken custody and control as required within s 101(b)` `the appointee has taken the property of the corporation into their custody and control in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed`

@export Has the appointee kept the corporation's money in a bank account as required (s 101(c))?
GIVEN `the appointee has opened and maintains a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has opened and maintains a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee kept the corporation's money in a bank account as required` IF `the appointee has opened and maintains the bank account as required within s 101(c)` `the appointee has opened and maintains a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control`

@export Has the appointee kept detailed accounts (s 101(d))?
GIVEN `the appointee keeps detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee keeps detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee kept detailed accounts` IF `the appointee keeps the detailed accounts as required within s 101(d)` `the appointee keeps detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`

@export Has the appointee made the accounts available for inspection as required (s 101(e))?
GIVEN `the appointee keeps accounts of their administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee keeps accounts of their administration?
      `the accounts are available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the accounts are available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee made the accounts available for inspection as required` IF `the appointee makes the accounts available as required within s 101(e)` `the appointee keeps accounts of their administration` `the accounts are available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation`

@export Has the appointee prepared financial statements as required (s 101(f))?
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the appointment?
      `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (first)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration
      `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (second)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration
      `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (third)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
      `the statements are in the form required by section 155 as far as is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statements are in the form required by section 155 as far as is practicable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee prepared financial statements as required` IF `the appointee has prepared the financial statements as required within s 101(f)` `the date of the appointment` `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration as a list` `the day asked about` `the statements are in the form required by section 155 as far as is practicable`
    WHERE
        `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration as a list` MEANS LIST `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (first)`, `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (second)`, `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration (third)`

@export Has the appointee rendered the final account (s 101(g))?
GIVEN `the appointee has completed their duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has completed their duties?
      `the appointee has rendered a final account of their administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointee has rendered a final account of their administration?
      `the final account is in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph 101(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the final account is in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph 101(f)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the appointee rendered the final account` IF `the appointee has rendered the final account as required within s 101(g)` `the appointee has completed their duties` `the appointee has rendered a final account of their administration` `the final account is in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph 101(f)`


§ `Directors and officers (Part X, ss 102 to 125)`

§§ `Management, the number of directors and by-laws (ss 102 and 103)`

@export Must the directors manage the corporation, or does a unanimous shareholder agreement take that from them (s 102(1))?
GIVEN `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a unanimous shareholder agreement?
      `the agreement restricts the powers of the directors in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the agreement restricts the powers of the directors in the matter?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors manage the corporation, or does a unanimous shareholder agreement take that from them` IF `the directors must manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs within s 102(1)` `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement` `the agreement restricts the powers of the directors in the matter`

@export Does our board have enough directors (s 102(2))?
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors?
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is a distributing corporation?
      `any of the issued securities of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any of the issued securities of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person?
      `the number of directors who are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors who are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our board have enough directors` IF `the number of directors complies within s 102(2)` `the number of directors` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `any of the issued securities of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` `the number of directors who are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates`

@export May the directors make, amend or repeal a by-law by resolution (s 103(1))?
GIVEN `the by-law regulates the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the by-law regulates the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors make, amend or repeal a by-law by resolution` IF `the directors may make, amend or repeal the by-law by resolution within s 103(1)` `the by-law regulates the business or affairs of the corporation` `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

@export Must the directors submit the by-law to the shareholders at the next meeting (s 103(2))?
GIVEN `the directors made, amended or repealed a by-law under subsection 103(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors made, amended or repealed a by-law under subsection 103(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors submit the by-law to the shareholders at the next meeting` IF `the directors must submit the by-law to the shareholders at the next meeting within s 103(2)` `the directors made, amended or repealed a by-law under subsection 103(1)`

@export May the shareholders confirm, reject or amend the by-law the directors made (s 103(2))?
GIVEN `the by-law was submitted to the shareholders under subsection 103(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the by-law was submitted to the shareholders under subsection 103(2)?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is an ordinary resolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders confirm, reject or amend the by-law the directors made` IF `the shareholders may confirm, reject or amend the by-law within s 103(2)` `the by-law was submitted to the shareholders under subsection 103(2)` `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`

@export Is the by-law the directors made in effect (s 103(3))?
GIVEN `what the shareholders did` IS A `What the shareholders did with a by-law` @desc What did the shareholders do with the by-law the directors made?
      `the next meeting of shareholders has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the next meeting of shareholders has been held?
      `the directors submitted the by-law at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors submitted the by-law at that meeting?
GIVETH A `Status of a by-law made by the directors`
DECIDE `Is the by-law the directors made in effect` IS `the status of the by-law within s 103(3)` `what the shareholders did` `the next meeting of shareholders has been held` `the directors submitted the by-law at that meeting`

@export Is a later resolution of the directors on the same subject effective (s 103(4))?
GIVEN `the earlier by-law, amendment or repeal ceased to be effective under subsection 103(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the earlier by-law, amendment or repeal ceased to be effective under subsection 103(4)?
      `the later resolution has substantially the same purpose or effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the later resolution has substantially the same purpose or effect?
      `the shareholders have confirmed the later resolution or confirmed it as amended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shareholders have confirmed the later resolution or confirmed it as amended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a later resolution of the directors on the same subject effective` IF `the later resolution of the directors is effective within s 103(4)` `the earlier by-law, amendment or repeal ceased to be effective under subsection 103(4)` `the later resolution has substantially the same purpose or effect` `the shareholders have confirmed the later resolution or confirmed it as amended`

@export May I, as a shareholder, propose to make, amend or repeal a by-law (s 103(5))?
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proposal is made in accordance with section 137?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a shareholder, propose to make, amend or repeal a by-law` IF `the shareholder may make a proposal to make, amend or repeal a by-law within s 103(5)` `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137`

§§ `The organization meeting (s 104)`

@export Does the Act require a first meeting of directors of our corporation (s 104(1))?
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate of incorporation has been issued?
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)?
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act require a first meeting of directors of our corporation` IF `a meeting of the directors must be held within s 104(1)` `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`

@export What business may the directors transact at the organization meeting (s 104(1))?
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate of incorporation has been issued?
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)?
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Business the directors may transact at the organization meeting`)
DECIDE `What business may the directors transact at the organization meeting` IS `the business the directors may transact at the organization meeting within s 104(1)` `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`

@export Does the first-meeting requirement not apply because we came by amalgamation or continuance (s 104(2))?
GIVEN `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)?
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the first-meeting requirement not apply because we came by amalgamation or continuance` IF `subsection 104(1) does not apply to the body corporate within s 104(2)` `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`

@export May I call the organization meeting (s 104(3))?
GIVEN `the person is an incorporator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an incorporator?
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I call the organization meeting` IF `the person may call the meeting within s 104(3)` `the person is an incorporator` `the person is a director`

@export Have I called the organization meeting as the Act requires (s 104(3))?
GIVEN `the person is an incorporator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an incorporator?
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director?
      `the notice is given by mail to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is given by mail to each director?
      `the notice states the time and place of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the time and place of the meeting?
      `the number of days of notice given` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days of notice given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I called the organization meeting as the Act requires` IF `the meeting is called as required within s 104(3)` `the person is an incorporator` `the person is a director` `the notice is given by mail to each director` `the notice states the time and place of the meeting` `the number of days of notice given`

§§ `Who may be a director (s 105)`

@export Am I disqualified from being a director (s 105(1))?
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the person in years?
      `the person is incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is incapable?
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an individual?
      `the person has the status of bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has the status of bankrupt?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified from being a director` IF `the person is disqualified from being a director within s 105(1)` `the age of the person in years` `the person is incapable` `the person is an individual` `the person has the status of bankrupt`

@export Must I hold shares in order to be a director (s 105(2))?
GIVEN `the articles provide that a director must hold shares issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide that a director must hold shares issued by the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I hold shares in order to be a director` IF `a director is required to hold shares within s 105(2)` `the articles provide that a director must hold shares issued by the corporation`

@export Is our corporation one that needs a majority of resident Canadian directors (s 105(3.1))?
GIVEN `the corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a business sector prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a business sector prescribed by the regulations?
      `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation, individually or to engage in an activity in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation, individually or to engage in an activity in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control?
      `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our corporation one that needs a majority of resident Canadian directors` IF `a corporation is referred to in s 105(3.1)` `the corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a business sector prescribed by the regulations` `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation, individually or to engage in an activity in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control`

@export Does the holding-corporation exception apply to us (s 105(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a holding corporation referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is a holding corporation referred to in subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the revenues earned in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the revenues earned in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries in dollars?
      `the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars?
      `the figures are those shown in the financial statements described in paragraph 105(4)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the figures are those shown in the financial statements described in paragraph 105(4)(a) or (b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the holding-corporation exception apply to us` IF `the exception applies within s 105(4)` `the corporation is a holding corporation referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` `the revenues earned in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries in dollars` `the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars` `the figures are those shown in the financial statements described in paragraph 105(4)(a) or (b)`

@export How many of our directors must be resident Canadians (s 105(3))?
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors?
      `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)?
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a figure to give: the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified? (yes or no)
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (the value)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation? (if you answered no above, give any figure; it is ignored)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of our directors must be resident Canadians` IS `the least number of resident Canadian directors required within s 105(3)` `the number of directors` `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does our board meet the resident Canadian requirement (s 105(3))?
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors?
      `the number of the directors who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the directors who are resident Canadians?
      `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)?
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a figure to give: the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified? (yes or no)
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (the value)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation? (if you answered no above, give any figure; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our board meet the resident Canadian requirement` IF `the residency requirement is met within s 105(3)` `the number of directors` `the number of the directors who are resident Canadians` `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Electing directors, their terms and cumulative voting (ss 106 and 107)`

@export Have we, as incorporators, sent the notice of directors (s 106(1))?
GIVEN `the notice of directors is sent at the time of sending the articles of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice of directors is sent at the time of sending the articles of incorporation?
      `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is in the form that the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we, as incorporators, sent the notice of directors` IF `the incorporators have sent the notice of directors as required within s 106(1)` `the notice of directors is sent at the time of sending the articles of incorporation` `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes`

@export Must the Director file the notice of directors (s 106(1))?
GIVEN `the Director has received the notice of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Director has received the notice of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director file the notice of directors` IF `the Director must file the notice of directors within s 106(1)` `the Director has received the notice of directors`

@export Do I hold office on this day as a director named in the notice (s 106(2))?
GIVEN `the director is named in the notice of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director is named in the notice of directors?
      `the date the certificate of incorporation was issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the certificate of incorporation was issued?
      `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held? (yes or no)
      `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the first meeting of shareholders? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I hold office on this day as a director named in the notice` IF `the director named in the notice holds office on the day asked about within s 106(2)` `the director is named in the notice of directors` `the date the certificate of incorporation was issued` `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Must the shareholders elect directors at this meeting (s 106(3))?
GIVEN `the meeting is the first meeting of shareholders or an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is the first meeting of shareholders or an annual meeting?
      `an election of directors is required at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an election of directors is required at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the shareholders elect directors at this meeting` IF `the shareholders must elect directors by ordinary resolution within s 106(3)` `the meeting is the first meeting of shareholders or an annual meeting` `an election of directors is required at the meeting`

@export At the close of which annual meeting may a director's term end (s 106(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is a distributing corporation?
      `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations or in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations or in circumstances prescribed by the regulations?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `At the close of which annual meeting may a director's term end` IS `the latest annual meeting at whose close a director's term may end within s 106(3)` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations or in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` `the articles provide for cumulative voting`

@export Must a separate vote be taken for each candidate (s 106(3.3))?
GIVEN `the election of directors is for a corporation prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the election of directors is for a corporation prescribed by the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a separate vote be taken for each candidate` IF `a separate vote must be taken for each candidate within s 106(3.3)` `the election of directors is for a corporation prescribed by the regulations`

@export Has the candidate won the majority needed to be elected (s 106(3.4))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is a distributing corporation?
      `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations prescribed by the regulations?
      `there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board?
      `the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy?
      `the votes cast against the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the votes cast against the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy?
      `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a figure to give: the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority? (yes or no)
      `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority (the value)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes in favour that the articles require? (if you answered no above, give any figure; it is ignored)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the candidate won the majority needed to be elected` IS `the candidate receives the majority needed to be elected within s 106(3.4)` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations prescribed by the regulations` `there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board` `the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` `the votes cast against the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Must all the directors elected at the meeting hold office for the same term (s 106(4))?
GIVEN `directors are elected at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that directors are elected at a meeting of shareholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must all the directors elected at the meeting hold office for the same term` IS `all directors elected at the meeting must hold office for the same term within s 106(4)` `directors are elected at a meeting of shareholders`

@export Do I still hold office as a director who was elected without a stated term (s 106(5))?
GIVEN `the director was elected for an expressly stated term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was elected for an expressly stated term?
      `the date of the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the election` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the election?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I still hold office as a director who was elected without a stated term` IS `the director still holds office on the day asked about within s 106(5)` `the director was elected for an expressly stated term` `the date of the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the election` `the day asked about`

@export Do I continue in office as an incumbent director because no election was held (s 106(6))?
GIVEN `directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders?
      `the director is an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director is an incumbent director?
      `their successors have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that their successors have been elected?
      `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I continue in office as an incumbent director because no election was held` IF `the incumbent director continues in office within s 106(6)` `directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders` `the director is an incumbent director` `their successors have been elected` `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected`

@export May I continue in office after I was a candidate and was not elected (s 106(6.1))?
GIVEN `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected?
      `the day of the election` IS A DATE @desc What is the day of the election?
      `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been? (yes or no)
      `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which their successor is appointed or elected? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I continue in office after I was a candidate and was not elected` IF `the incumbent director who was not elected may continue in office on the day asked about within s 106(6.1)` `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` `the day of the election` `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export May the directors elected at a failed meeting exercise all the powers of the directors (s 106(7))?
GIVEN `the meeting fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles?
      `the failure is due to a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the failure is due to a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates?
      `the failure is due to a lack of a majority referred to in subsection 106(3.4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the failure is due to a lack of a majority referred to in subsection 106(3.4)?
      `the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors elected at a failed meeting exercise all the powers of the directors` IF `the directors elected may exercise all the powers of the directors within s 106(7)` `the meeting fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles` `the failure is due to a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates` `the failure is due to a lack of a majority referred to in subsection 106(3.4)` `the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum`

@export May the directors appoint additional directors (s 106(8))?
GIVEN `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles otherwise provide?
      `the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the number of additional directors already appointed under subsection 106(8)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of additional directors already appointed under subsection 106(8)?
      `the number of additional directors proposed to be appointed` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of additional directors proposed to be appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors appoint additional directors` IF `the directors may appoint the additional directors within s 106(8)` `the articles otherwise provide` `the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders` `the number of additional directors already appointed under subsection 106(8)` `the number of additional directors proposed to be appointed`

@export May an additional director appointed by the directors hold office until this day (s 106(8))?
GIVEN `the date of the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an additional director appointed by the directors hold office until this day` IF `the additional director may hold office on the day asked about within s 106(8)` `the date of the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders` `the day asked about`

@export May I be appointed as a director after I was a candidate and was not elected (s 106(8.1))?
GIVEN `the individual was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected?
      `the appointment is in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appointment is in circumstances prescribed by the regulations?
      `the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required has been held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be appointed as a director after I was a candidate and was not elected` IS `the individual may be appointed as a director under subsection 106(8) or 111(1) within s 106(8.1)` `the individual was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` `the appointment is in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` `the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required has been held`

@export Am I a director, given how I was elected or appointed (s 106(9))?
GIVEN `the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place?
      `the individual refused to hold office as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual refused to hold office as a director?
      `the date of the election or appointment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the election or appointment?
      `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did? (yes or no)
      `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the individual has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a director, given how I was elected or appointed` IF `the individual is a director within s 106(9)` `the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place` `the individual refused to hold office as a director` `the date of the election or appointment` `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did as the rule reads it` `the individual has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment`
    WHERE
        `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Do our articles meet the requirement for a fixed number of directors under cumulative voting (s 107(a))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the articles require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do our articles meet the requirement for a fixed number of directors under cumulative voting` IF `the articles meet the requirement for a fixed number of directors within s 107(a)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the articles require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors`

@export How many votes may I cast in an election of directors under cumulative voting (s 107(b))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder?
      `the number of directors to be elected` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors to be elected?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes may I cast in an election of directors under cumulative voting` IS `the number of votes the shareholder may cast within s 107(b)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder` `the number of directors to be elected`

@export Is my distribution of votes among the candidates permitted (s 107(b))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the number of votes the shareholder may cast` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes the shareholder may cast?
      `the votes given to each candidate (first)` IS A NUMBER @desc Give a number, up to three; use 0 if fewer apply: the votes given to each candidate
      `the votes given to each candidate (second)` IS A NUMBER @desc Give a number, up to three; use 0 if fewer apply: the votes given to each candidate
      `the votes given to each candidate (third)` IS A NUMBER @desc Give a number, up to three; use 0 if fewer apply: the votes given to each candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my distribution of votes among the candidates permitted` IF `the shareholder's distribution of votes is permitted within s 107(b)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the number of votes the shareholder may cast` `the votes given to each candidate as a list`
    WHERE
        `the votes given to each candidate as a list` MEANS LIST `the votes given to each candidate (first)`, `the votes given to each candidate (second)`, `the votes given to each candidate (third)`

@export Must a separate vote be taken for each candidate under cumulative voting (s 107(c))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a separate vote be taken for each candidate under cumulative voting` IF `a separate vote must be taken for each candidate within s 107(c)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution`

@export How many votes does each candidate get from me where I did not say how to divide them (s 107(d))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the number of candidates the shareholder voted for` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of candidates the shareholder voted for?
      `the shareholder specified the distribution of votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shareholder specified the distribution of votes?
      `the number of votes the shareholder cast` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes the shareholder cast?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes does each candidate get from me where I did not say how to divide them` IS `the votes each candidate receives from the shareholder within s 107(d)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the number of candidates the shareholder voted for` `the shareholder specified the distribution of votes` `the number of votes the shareholder cast`

@export How many candidates are eliminated for lack of votes (s 107(e))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the number of candidates nominated for director` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of candidates nominated for director?
      `the number of positions to be filled` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of positions to be filled?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many candidates are eliminated for lack of votes` IS `the number of candidates to be eliminated within s 107(e)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the number of candidates nominated for director` `the number of positions to be filled`

@export Does a director cease to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting under cumulative voting (s 107(f))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a director cease to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting under cumulative voting` IF `a director ceases to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting following election within s 107(f)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting`

@export Is the vote needed to remove a director under cumulative voting met (s 107(g))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the number of votes cast in favour of the director's removal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes cast in favour of the director's removal?
      `the number of votes cast against the motion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes cast against the motion?
      `the number of directors required by the articles` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors required by the articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the vote needed to remove a director under cumulative voting met` IS `the vote needed to remove the director is met within s 107(g)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the number of votes cast in favour of the director's removal` `the number of votes cast against the motion` `the number of directors required by the articles`

@export Is the vote needed to decrease the number of directors under cumulative voting met (s 107(h))?
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors?
      `the number of votes cast against the motion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of votes cast against the motion?
      `the number of directors required by the articles` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors required by the articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the vote needed to decrease the number of directors under cumulative voting met` IS `the vote needed to decrease the number of directors is met within s 107(h)` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors` `the number of votes cast against the motion` `the number of directors required by the articles`

§§ `Leaving office, removal and a director's right to be heard (ss 108 to 110)`

@export Have I ceased to be a director (s 108(1))?
GIVEN `the director has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has died?
      `the director has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has resigned?
      `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is an ordinary resolution?
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders?
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)?
      `the director has become disqualified under subsection 105(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has become disqualified under subsection 105(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I ceased to be a director` IF `the director ceases to hold office within s 108(1)` `the director has died` `the director has resigned` `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` `the director has become disqualified under subsection 105(1)`

@export On what date does my resignation take effect (s 108(2))?
GIVEN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation?
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified? (yes or no)
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date specified in the resignation? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my resignation take effect` IS `the date a resignation becomes effective within s 108(2)` `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has my resignation taken effect on this day (s 108(2))?
GIVEN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation?
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified? (yes or no)
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date specified in the resignation? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my resignation taken effect on this day` IF `the resignation has become effective on the day asked about within s 108(2)` `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified as the rule reads it` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export May the shareholders remove a director by ordinary resolution at a special meeting (s 109(1))?
GIVEN `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is an ordinary resolution?
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders remove a director by ordinary resolution at a special meeting` IF `the shareholders may remove the director within s 109(1)` `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`

@export May a director elected by a class or series be removed (s 109(2))?
GIVEN `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is an ordinary resolution?
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a director elected by a class or series be removed` IF `a director elected by a class or series may be removed within s 109(2)` `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`

@export Has the director been removed in accordance with s 109 (s 109(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is an ordinary resolution?
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders?
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the director been removed in accordance with s 109 (s 109(1) and (2))` IF `the director is removed in accordance with section 109 within s 109(1)` `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`

@export May the vacancy be filled at the meeting at which the director is removed (s 109(3))?
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy was created by the removal of a director?
      `the meeting is the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the vacancy be filled at the meeting at which the director is removed` IF `the vacancy may be filled at the meeting at which the director is removed within s 109(3)` `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` `the meeting is the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed`

@export May the vacancy be filled under s 111 because it was not filled at the meeting (s 109(3))?
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy was created by the removal of a director?
      `the vacancy was filled at the meeting at which the director was removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy was filled at the meeting at which the director was removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the vacancy be filled under s 111 because it was not filled at the meeting` IF `the vacancy may be filled under section 111 within s 109(3)` `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` `the vacancy was filled at the meeting at which the director was removed`

@export Does s 109(4) not apply to me because of the position I hold (s 109(5))?
GIVEN `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person?
      `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional?
      `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services?
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a answer to give: the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)? (yes or no)
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (the value)` IS A `Kind of person who takes part in management under s 109(5)(c)` @desc What is the kind of person the person is? (if you answered no above, give any answer; it is ignored)
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security?
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 109(4) not apply to me because of the position I hold` IF `subsection 109(4) does not apply to the person within s 109(5)` `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) as the rule reads it` `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate`
    WHERE
        `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I deemed to be a director because I manage the corporation after all the directors have gone (s 109(4))?
GIVEN `all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement?
      `the person manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation?
      `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person?
      `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional?
      `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services?
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a answer to give: the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)? (yes or no)
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (the value)` IS A `Kind of person who takes part in management under s 109(5)(c)` @desc What is the kind of person the person is? (if you answered no above, give any answer; it is ignored)
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security?
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to be a director because I manage the corporation after all the directors have gone` IF `the person is deemed to be a director within s 109(4)` `all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement` `the person manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) as the rule reads it` `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate`
    WHERE
        `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c) (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I, as a director, entitled to notice of, to attend and to be heard at a meeting of shareholders (s 110(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director of the corporation?
      `the meeting is a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the meeting is a meeting of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a director, entitled to notice of, to attend and to be heard at a meeting of shareholders` IF `the director is entitled to receive notice of, attend and be heard at the meeting within s 110(1)` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the meeting is a meeting of shareholders`

@export May I submit a written statement giving my reasons for resigning or for opposing a proposed action (s 110(2))?
GIVEN `the director resigns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director resigns?
      `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office?
      `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I submit a written statement giving my reasons for resigning or for opposing a proposed action` IF `the director is entitled to submit a written statement within s 110(2)` `the director resigns` `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office` `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director`

@export To whom must the corporation send a copy of my statement (s 110(3))?
GIVEN `the director has submitted a statement under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has submitted a statement under subsection 110(2)?
      `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150?
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
DECIDE `To whom must the corporation send a copy of my statement` IS `those to whom the corporation must forthwith send a copy of the statement within s 110(3)` `the director has submitted a statement under subsection 110(2)` `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150`

@export Is the corporation, or a person acting for it, protected from liability for circulating my statement (s 110(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation or the person acting on its behalf circulated the statement in compliance with subsection 110(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation or the person acting on its behalf circulated the statement in compliance with subsection 110(3)?
      `the liability is alleged by reason only of circulating the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the liability is alleged by reason only of circulating the statement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation, or a person acting for it, protected from liability for circulating my statement` IF `the corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs no liability within s 110(4)` `the corporation or the person acting on its behalf circulated the statement in compliance with subsection 110(3)` `the liability is alleged by reason only of circulating the statement`

§§ `Filling a vacancy and changing the number of directors (ss 111 to 113)`

@export Who alone may fill the vacancy where our articles say shareholders must fill it (s 111(4))?
GIVEN `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders?
      `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who alone may fill a vacancy under s 111(4)`
DECIDE `Who alone may fill the vacancy where our articles say shareholders must fill it` IS `who alone may fill the vacancy within s 111(4)` `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders` `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect`

@export May a quorum of directors fill the vacancy (s 111(1))?
GIVEN `there is a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a quorum of directors?
      `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors?
      `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles?
      `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect?
      `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a quorum of directors fill the vacancy` IF `a quorum of directors may fill the vacancy within s 111(1)` `there is a quorum of directors` `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect` `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders`

@export Must the directors in office call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy (s 111(2))?
GIVEN `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is not a quorum of directors?
      `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors in office call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy` IF `the directors then in office must without delay call a special meeting of shareholders within s 111(2)` `there is not a quorum of directors` `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles`

@export May I, as a shareholder, call the meeting to fill the vacancy (s 111(2))?
GIVEN `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is not a quorum of directors?
      `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles?
      `the directors then in office failed to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors then in office failed to call a meeting?
      `there are no directors then in office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there are no directors then in office?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a shareholder, call the meeting to fill the vacancy` IF `any shareholder may call the meeting within s 111(2)` `there is not a quorum of directors` `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` `the directors then in office failed to call a meeting` `there are no directors then in office`

@export May the remaining class directors fill the vacancy among directors elected by their class (s 111(3))?
GIVEN `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors?
      `a vacancy occurs among those directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a vacancy occurs among those directors?
      `there are remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there are remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series?
      `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series?
      `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series?
      `the articles provide that the vacancy shall only be filled by a vote of the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide that the vacancy shall only be filled by a vote of the holders of that class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the remaining class directors fill the vacancy among directors elected by their class` IF `the remaining directors elected by that class or series may fill the vacancy within s 111(3)(a)` `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` `a vacancy occurs among those directors` `there are remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series` `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series` `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series` `the articles provide that the vacancy shall only be filled by a vote of the holders of that class or series`

@export May I, as a holder of that class, call a meeting of the class to fill the vacancy (s 111(3))?
GIVEN `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors?
      `a vacancy occurs among those directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a vacancy occurs among those directors?
      `there are no remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there are no remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a holder of that class, call a meeting of the class to fill the vacancy` IF `any holder of shares of that class or series may call a meeting of the holders within s 111(3)(b)` `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` `a vacancy occurs among those directors` `there are no remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series`

@export Do I hold office on this day as the director who filled a vacancy (s 111(5))?
GIVEN `the director was appointed or elected to fill a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was appointed or elected to fill a vacancy?
      `the date of the appointment or election` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the appointment or election?
      `the last day of the unexpired term of the predecessor` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the unexpired term of the predecessor?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the day asked about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I hold office on this day as the director who filled a vacancy` IF `the director appointed or elected to fill a vacancy holds office on the day asked about within s 111(5)` `the director was appointed or elected to fill a vacancy` `the date of the appointment or election` `the last day of the unexpired term of the predecessor` `the day asked about`

@export May the shareholders amend the articles to change the number of directors (s 112(1))?
GIVEN `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)?
      `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders amend the articles to change the number of directors` IF `the shareholders may amend the articles to change the number of directors within s 112(1)` `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director`

@export May the shareholders elect the number of directors the amendment authorizes at the same meeting (s 112(2))?
GIVEN `the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles?
      `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors?
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles provide for cumulative voting?
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)?
      `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders elect the number of directors the amendment authorizes at the same meeting` IF `the shareholders may elect the number of directors authorized by the amendment at the meeting within s 112(2)` `the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles` `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` `the articles provide for cumulative voting` `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director`

@export As of what date are the articles deemed amended for that election (s 112(2))?
GIVEN `a certificate of amendment has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of amendment has been issued?
      `the date the shareholders adopt the amendment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the shareholders adopt the amendment?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `As of what date are the articles deemed amended for that election` IS `the date as of which the articles are deemed amended within s 112(2)` `a certificate of amendment has been issued` `the date the shareholders adopt the amendment`

@export By what day must the corporation tell the Director of a change among its directors (s 113(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation tell the Director of a change among its directors` IS `the last day for the corporation to send the notice to the Director within s 113(1)` `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director`

@export Has the corporation sent the Director the notice of change as required (s 113(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director?
      `the date the corporation sent the notice to the Director` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the corporation sent the notice to the Director?
      `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is in the form that the Director fixes?
      `the notice sets out the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice sets out the change?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation sent the Director the notice of change as required` IF `the corporation has sent the notice to the Director as required within s 113(1)` `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director` `the date the corporation sent the notice to the Director` `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes` `the notice sets out the change`

@export Must the Director file the notice of change (s 113(1))?
GIVEN `the Director has received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Director has received the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director file the notice of change` IF `the Director must file the notice of change within s 113(1)` `the Director has received the notice`

@export Have I, as a director, told the corporation of my change of address in time (s 113(1.1))?
GIVEN `the date the director changed their address` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director changed their address?
      `the date the director sent the corporation notice of the change` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director sent the corporation notice of the change?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I, as a director, told the corporation of my change of address in time` IF `the director has sent the corporation notice of the change of address as required within s 113(1.1)` `the date the director changed their address` `the date the director sent the corporation notice of the change`

@export May I apply to a court to make the corporation send the notice of change (s 113(2))?
GIVEN `the person is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an interested person?
      `the person is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court to make the corporation send the notice of change` IF `the person may apply to a court for an order requiring the corporation to comply with subsection 113(1) within s 113(2)` `the person is an interested person` `the person is the Director`

@export May the court order the corporation to comply with the notice requirement (s 113(2))?
GIVEN `a person entitled to do so under subsection 113(2) has applied to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a person entitled to do so under subsection 113(2) has applied to a court?
      `the corporation has not complied with subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation has not complied with subsection 113(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order the corporation to comply with the notice requirement` IF `the court may order the corporation to comply and make any further order it thinks fit within s 113(2)` `a person entitled to do so under subsection 113(2) has applied to a court` `the corporation has not complied with subsection 113(1)`

§§ `Meetings of directors (s 114)`

@export May the directors meet at any place and on such notice as the by-laws require (s 114(1))?
GIVEN `the articles or by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles or by-laws otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors meet at any place and on such notice as the by-laws require` IF `the directors may meet at any place and on such notice as the by-laws require within s 114(1)` `the articles or by-laws otherwise provide`

@export Is there a quorum of directors (s 114(2))?
GIVEN `the number of directors, or the minimum number of directors, required by the articles` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors, or the minimum number of directors, required by the articles?
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present?
      `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a figure to give: the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one? (yes or no)
      `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one (the value)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum? (if you answered no above, give any figure; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a quorum of directors` IF `there is a quorum of directors within s 114(2)` `the number of directors, or the minimum number of directors, required by the articles` `the number of directors present` `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export May a quorum of directors exercise all the powers despite a vacancy (s 114(2))?
GIVEN `there is a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a quorum of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a quorum of directors exercise all the powers despite a vacancy` IF `a quorum of directors may exercise all the powers of the directors despite any vacancy within s 114(2)` `there is a quorum of directors`

@export May the directors present transact business, given how many are resident Canadians (s 114(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies?
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors of the corporation?
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present?
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present who are resident Canadians?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors present transact business, given how many are resident Canadians` IF `the directors may transact business under subsection 114(3) within s 114(3)` `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` `the number of directors of the corporation` `the number of directors present` `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians`

@export May the directors transact business although too few resident Canadians are present, because an absent one approves (s 114(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies?
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors of the corporation?
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present?
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present who are resident Canadians?
      `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors transact business although too few resident Canadians are present, because an absent one approves` IF `the directors may transact business despite subsection 114(3) within s 114(4)` `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` `the number of directors of the corporation` `the number of directors present` `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting`

@export May the directors transact business at this meeting (s 114(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies?
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)?
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors of the corporation?
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present?
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors present who are resident Canadians?
      `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors transact business at this meeting (s 114(3) and (4))` IF `the directors may transact business at the meeting within s 114(3) and (4)` `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` `the number of directors of the corporation` `the number of directors present` `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting`

@export Must the notice of the meeting specify this matter (s 114(5))?
GIVEN `the matter is one referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is one referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting?
      `the by-laws require the notice to specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the by-laws require the notice to specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the notice of the meeting specify this matter` IF `the notice of the meeting must specify the matter within s 114(5)` `the matter is one referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting` `the by-laws require the notice to specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted`

@export Have I waived notice of the meeting (s 114(6))?
GIVEN `the director waived the notice in some manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director waived the notice in some manner?
      `the director attended the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director attended the meeting?
      `the director attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I waived notice of the meeting` IF `the director has waived notice of the meeting within s 114(6)` `the director waived the notice in some manner` `the director attended the meeting` `the director attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called`

@export Is notice of the adjourned meeting not required (s 114(7))?
GIVEN `the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is notice of the adjourned meeting not required` IF `notice of the adjourned meeting of directors is not required within s 114(7)` `the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting`

@export May our one director constitute a meeting (s 114(8))?
GIVEN `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our one director constitute a meeting` IF `the one director may constitute a meeting within s 114(8)` `the number of directors of the corporation`

@export May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other communication facility (s 114(9))?
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the by-laws otherwise provide?
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any?
      `all the directors of the corporation consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all the directors of the corporation consent?
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other communication facility` IF `the director may participate by a communication facility within s 114(9)` `the by-laws otherwise provide` `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` `all the directors of the corporation consent` `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting`

@export Am I deemed present at the meeting because I take part by communication facility (s 114(9))?
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the by-laws otherwise provide?
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any?
      `all the directors of the corporation consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all the directors of the corporation consent?
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting?
      `the director participates in the meeting by that means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director participates in the meeting by that means?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed present at the meeting because I take part by communication facility` IF `the director is deemed present at the meeting within s 114(9)` `the by-laws otherwise provide` `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` `all the directors of the corporation consent` `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` `the director participates in the meeting by that means`

§§ `Delegation, validity of acts and resolutions in writing (ss 115 to 117)`

@export May the directors appoint a managing director or a committee and delegate powers to it (s 115(1))?
GIVEN `the delegate` IS A `Delegate of the powers of the directors` @desc What is the delegate?
      `the delegate is appointed from the number of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the delegate is appointed from the number of the directors?
      `the managing director is a resident Canadian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the managing director is a resident Canadian?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors appoint a managing director or a committee and delegate powers to it` IF `the directors may appoint the delegate and delegate powers to it within s 115(1)` `the delegate` `the delegate is appointed from the number of the directors` `the managing director is a resident Canadian`

@export May a managing director or committee exercise this power (s 115(3))?
GIVEN `the power` IS A `Power of the directors` @desc What is the power?
      `the directors have authorized the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have authorized the act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a managing director or committee exercise this power` IF `the managing director or committee has authority to exercise the power within s 115(3)` `the power` `the directors have authorized the act`

@export Is an act of mine as a director or officer valid despite an irregularity in my election or a defect in my qualification (s 116)?
GIVEN `the act is an act of a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the act is an act of a director or officer?
      `the ground alleged is an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the ground alleged is an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an act of mine as a director or officer valid despite an irregularity in my election or a defect in my qualification` IF `the irregularity or defect does not invalidate the act within s 116` `the act is an act of a director or officer` `the ground alleged is an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification`

@export Is a resolution in writing as valid as one passed at a meeting (s 117(1))?
GIVEN `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is in writing?
      `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a resolution in writing as valid as one passed at a meeting` IF `the written resolution is as valid as if passed at a meeting within s 117(1)` `the resolution is in writing` `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it`

@export Must a copy of the written resolution be kept with the minutes (s 117(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the resolution is in writing?
      `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a copy of the written resolution be kept with the minutes` IF `a copy of the resolution must be kept with the minutes within s 117(2)` `the resolution is in writing` `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it`

@export Is the minute entry proof of the declared result without proof of the votes (s 117(3))?
GIVEN `the minutes record that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the minutes record that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated?
      `a ballot is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a ballot is demanded?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the minute entry proof of the declared result without proof of the votes` IF `the minute entry is proof of the declared result without proof of the votes within s 117(3)` `the minutes record that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated` `a ballot is demanded` `there is evidence to the contrary`

§§ `What a director owes and can be made to pay (ss 118 and 119)`

@export What amount must I make good for a share issued for property worth less than its price (s 118(1))?
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25?
      `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the share was issued for a consideration other than money?
      `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution?
      `the consideration the corporation received in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the consideration the corporation received in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What amount must I make good for a share issued for property worth less than its price` IS `the amount the director must make good within s 118(1)` `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` `the consideration the corporation received in dollars`

@export Am I not liable because I did not know and could not reasonably have known the share was under-priced (s 118(6))?
GIVEN `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money?
      `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not liable because I did not know and could not reasonably have known the share was under-priced` IF `the director is not liable under subsection 118(1) within s 118(6)` `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it`

@export What do I owe after the defence of not knowing (s 118(1) and (6))?
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25?
      `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the share was issued for a consideration other than money?
      `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution?
      `the consideration the corporation received in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the consideration the corporation received in dollars?
      `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money?
      `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What do I owe after the defence of not knowing (s 118(1) and (6))` IS `the amount the director owes after the defence within s 118(1) and (6)` `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` `the consideration the corporation received in dollars` `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it`

@export What amount must I restore for an unlawful distribution or payment I voted for (s 118(2))?
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director voted for or consented to the resolution?
      `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a answer to give: the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e)? (yes or no)
      `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) (the value)` IS A `Act authorized contrary to the Act under s 118(2)` @desc What is the act the resolution authorized? (if you answered no above, give any answer; it is ignored)
      `the act was contrary to the section named for it in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the act was contrary to the section named for it in that paragraph?
      `the amount so distributed or paid in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount so distributed or paid in dollars?
      `the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What amount must I restore for an unlawful distribution or payment I voted for` IS `the amount the directors must restore within s 118(2)` `the director voted for or consented to the resolution` `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) as the rule reads it` `the act was contrary to the section named for it in that paragraph` `the amount so distributed or paid in dollars` `the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars`
    WHERE
        `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e) (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I entitled to contribution from the other directors who voted for the unlawful act (s 118(3))?
GIVEN `the director has satisfied a judgment rendered under section 118` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has satisfied a judgment rendered under section 118?
      `the other director voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other director voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to contribution from the other directors who voted for the unlawful act` IF `the director is entitled to contribution from the other director within s 118(3)` `the director has satisfied a judgment rendered under section 118` `the other director voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded`

@export May I apply to a court to make a shareholder or other recipient pay the money back to me (s 118(4))?
GIVEN `the director is liable under subsection 118(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director is liable under subsection 118(2)?
      `the money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court to make a shareholder or other recipient pay the money back to me` IF `the director may apply to a court for an order compelling the recipient to pay or deliver within s 118(4)` `the director is liable under subsection 118(2)` `the money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241`

@export Which orders may the court make on my application (s 118(5))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 118(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application has been made under subsection 118(4)?
      `the court is satisfied that it is equitable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court is satisfied that it is equitable to do so?
      `money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241?
      `the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 118(5)`
DECIDE `Which orders may the court make on my application` IS `the orders the court may make within s 118(5)` `an application has been made under subsection 118(4)` `the court is satisfied that it is equitable to do so` `money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241` `the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person`

@export Can an action to enforce liability under s 118 still be commenced (s 118(7))?
GIVEN `the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of?
      `the date the action to enforce the liability is commenced` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the action to enforce the liability is commenced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an action to enforce liability under s 118 still be commenced` IF `the action to enforce the liability may be commenced within s 118(7)` `the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of` `the date the action to enforce the liability is commenced`

@export How much am I liable to an employee for unpaid wages (s 119(1))?
GIVEN `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed?
      `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars?
      `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are six months of the employee's wages, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I liable to an employee for unpaid wages` IS `the amount the director is liable to the employee for within s 119(1)` `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars`

@export Is the condition in s 119(2)(a) met, so that I may be liable for the wages (s 119(2))?
GIVEN `the date the debt became due` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the debt became due?
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the corporation was sued for the debt? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the condition in s 119(2)(a) met, so that I may be liable for the wages` IF `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(a) is met within s 119(2)(a)` `the date the debt became due` `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was as the rule reads it` `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part`
    WHERE
        `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the condition in s 119(2)(b) met, so that I may be liable for the wages (s 119(2))?
GIVEN `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have? (yes or no)
      `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been? (yes or no)
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the corporation was dissolved? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been? (yes or no)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date a claim for the debt was proved? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the condition in s 119(2)(b) met, so that I may be liable for the wages` IF `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(b) is met within s 119(2)(b)` `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have as the rule reads it` `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been as the rule reads it` `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the condition in s 119(2)(c) met, so that I may be liable for the wages (s 119(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one? (yes or no)
      `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been? (yes or no)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date a claim for the debt was proved? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the condition in s 119(2)(c) met, so that I may be liable for the wages` IF `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(c) is met within s 119(2)(c)` `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one as the rule reads it` `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Are the conditions precedent to my liability for the wages met (s 119(2))?
GIVEN `the date the debt became due` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the debt became due?
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was? (yes or no)
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the corporation was sued for the debt? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part?
      `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have? (yes or no)
      `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been? (yes or no)
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the corporation was dissolved? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one? (yes or no)
      `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been? (yes or no)
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date a claim for the debt was proved? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the conditions precedent to my liability for the wages met` IF `the conditions precedent to the director's liability are met within s 119(2)` `the date the debt became due` `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was as the rule reads it` `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have as the rule reads it` `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been as the rule reads it` `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one as the rule reads it` `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Was I sued for the wages in time (s 119(3))?
GIVEN `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have? (yes or no)
      `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director ceased to be a director? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the director was sued` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director was sued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I sued for the wages in time` IF `the director was sued in time within s 119(3)` `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have as the rule reads it` `the date the director was sued`
    WHERE
        `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export How much can be recovered from me after execution against the corporation (s 119(4))?
GIVEN `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued?
      `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can be recovered from me after execution against the corporation` IS `the amount recoverable from a director after execution within s 119(4)` `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars`

@export How much can be recovered from me for the wages in all (s 119(1) and (4))?
GIVEN `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed?
      `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars?
      `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are six months of the employee's wages, in dollars?
      `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued?
      `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can be recovered from me for the wages in all (s 119(1) and (4))` IS `the amount recoverable from the director within s 119(1) and (4)` `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars` `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars`

@export What am I entitled to if I pay the employee's debt (s 119(5))?
GIVEN `the director pays a debt referred to in subsection 119(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director pays a debt referred to in subsection 119(1)?
      `the debt is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debt is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings?
      `a judgment has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a judgment has been obtained?
      `the director's claim arises in Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director's claim arises in Quebec?
GIVETH A LIST OF `What a director who pays a debt under s 119 is entitled to`
DECIDE `What am I entitled to if I pay the employee's debt` IS `what the paying director is entitled to within s 119(5)` `the director pays a debt referred to in subsection 119(1)` `the debt is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings` `a judgment has been obtained` `the director's claim arises in Quebec`

@export Am I entitled to contribution from the other directors who were liable for the wages (s 119(6))?
GIVEN `the director has satisfied a claim under section 119` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director has satisfied a claim under section 119?
      `the other director was liable for the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other director was liable for the claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to contribution from the other directors who were liable for the wages` IF `the director is entitled to contribution from the other director within s 119(6)` `the director has satisfied a claim under section 119` `the other director was liable for the claim`

§§ `Disclosing an interest in a contract (s 120)`

@export Must I disclose my interest in this contract or transaction (s 120(1))?
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction?
      `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed?
      `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a party to the contract or transaction?
      `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction?
      `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I disclose my interest in this contract or transaction` IF `the director or officer must disclose the interest within s 120(1)` `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction`

@export Is my disclosure made in the manner the Act requires (s 120(1))?
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to the corporation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disclosure is made to the corporation in writing?
      `the disclosure is made by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disclosure is made by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors?
      `the disclosure states the nature and extent of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disclosure states the nature and extent of the interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disclosure made in the manner the Act requires` IF `the disclosure is made in the manner required within s 120(1)` `the disclosure is made to the corporation in writing` `the disclosure is made by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors` `the disclosure states the nature and extent of the interest`

@export At which meeting must I, as a director, disclose my interest (s 120(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one? (yes or no)
      `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (first)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which meetings of directors are held
      `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (second)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which meetings of directors are held
      `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (third)` IS A DATE @desc Give a date, up to three; repeat a date if fewer apply: the dates on which meetings of directors are held
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `At which meeting must I, as a director, disclose my interest` IS `the latest meeting at which the director must disclose within s 120(2)` `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one as the rule reads it` `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do as the rule reads it` `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do as the rule reads it` `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do as the rule reads it` `the dates on which meetings of directors are held as a list`
    WHERE
        `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the dates on which meetings of directors are held as a list` MEANS LIST `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (first)`, `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (second)`, `the dates on which meetings of directors are held (third)`

@export By what day must I, as an officer who is not a director, disclose my interest (s 120(3))?
GIVEN `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do? (yes or no)
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I, as an officer who is not a director, disclose my interest` IS `the last day for the officer to disclose within s 120(3)` `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do as the rule reads it` `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do as the rule reads it` `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do as the rule reads it`
    WHERE
        `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export By what day must I disclose my interest in a contract that needs no approval (s 120(4))?
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders?
      `the date the director or officer becomes aware of the contract or transaction` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director or officer becomes aware of the contract or transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I disclose my interest in a contract that needs no approval` IS `the last day for the director or officer to disclose within s 120(4)` `the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders` `the date the director or officer becomes aware of the contract or transaction`

@export Is my disclosure not late (s 120(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one? (yes or no)
      `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4)? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the date the disclosure is made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the disclosure is made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disclosure not late (s 120(2) to (4))` IF `the disclosure is not late within s 120(2) to (4)` `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one as the rule reads it` `the date the disclosure is made`
    WHERE
        `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I barred from voting on the resolution to approve the contract (s 120(5))?
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction?
      `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed?
      `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a party to the contract or transaction?
      `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction?
      `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction?
      `the contract or transaction relates primarily to the director's remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction relates primarily to the director's remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate?
      `the contract or transaction is for indemnity or insurance under section 124` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is for indemnity or insurance under section 124?
      `the contract or transaction is with an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is with an affiliate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from voting on the resolution to approve the contract` IF `the director shall not vote on the resolution to approve the contract or transaction within s 120(5)` `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction` `the contract or transaction relates primarily to the director's remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate` `the contract or transaction is for indemnity or insurance under section 124` `the contract or transaction is with an affiliate`

@export Is the general notice a sufficient declaration of my interest (s 120(6))?
GIVEN `a general notice is given to the directors declaring that the director or officer is to be regarded as interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a general notice is given to the directors declaring that the director or officer is to be regarded as interested?
      `the contract or transaction is made with the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is made with the party?
      `the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph 120(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph 120(1)(b) or (c)?
      `the director or officer has a material interest in the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director or officer has a material interest in the party?
      `there has been a material change in the nature of the director's or the officer's interest in the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been a material change in the nature of the director's or the officer's interest in the party?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the general notice a sufficient declaration of my interest` IF `the general notice is a sufficient declaration of interest within s 120(6)` `a general notice is given to the directors declaring that the director or officer is to be regarded as interested` `the contract or transaction is made with the party` `the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph 120(1)(b) or (c)` `the director or officer has a material interest in the party` `there has been a material change in the nature of the director's or the officer's interest in the party`

@export May I, as a shareholder, examine the minutes and documents containing the disclosures (s 120(6.1))?
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a shareholder of the corporation?
      `the portion of the minutes, or the other document, contains disclosures under section 120` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the portion of the minutes, or the other document, contains disclosures under section 120?
      `the examination is during the usual business hours of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the examination is during the usual business hours of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a shareholder, examine the minutes and documents containing the disclosures` IF `the shareholder may examine the minutes or document within s 120(6.1)` `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` `the portion of the minutes, or the other document, contains disclosures under section 120` `the examination is during the usual business hours of the corporation`

@export Is the contract not invalid, and am I not accountable for the profit, under the usual standards (s 120(7))?
GIVEN `the ground is the director's or officer's interest, or that the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the ground is the director's or officer's interest, or that the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed?
      `disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections 120(1) to (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections 120(1) to (6)?
      `the directors approved the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors approved the contract or transaction?
      `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the contract not invalid, and am I not accountable for the profit, under the usual standards` IF `the contract is not invalid and the director or officer is not accountable for the profit within s 120(7)` `the ground is the director's or officer's interest, or that the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed` `disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections 120(1) to (6)` `the directors approved the contract or transaction` `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved`

@export Is the contract not invalid, and am I not accountable for the profit, because the shareholders confirmed it (s 120(7.1))?
GIVEN `the director or officer acted honestly and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director or officer acted honestly and in good faith?
      `the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders?
      `disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed?
      `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the contract not invalid, and am I not accountable for the profit, because the shareholders confirmed it` IF `the contract is not invalid and the director or officer is not accountable for the profit even if subsection 120(7) is not met within s 120(7.1)` `the director or officer acted honestly and in good faith` `the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders` `disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed` `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed`

@export Which orders may a court make against me or the contract if I failed to comply with s 120 (s 120(8))?
GIVEN `the director or officer fails to comply with section 120` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director or officer fails to comply with section 120?
      `the applicant is the corporation or one of its shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is the corporation or one of its shareholders?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 120(8)`
DECIDE `Which orders may a court make against me or the contract if I failed to comply with s 120` IS `the orders the court may make within s 120(8)` `the director or officer fails to comply with section 120` `the applicant is the corporation or one of its shareholders`

§§ `Officers, the duty of care and dissent (ss 121 to 123)`

@export Do the directors have this power over officers (s 121(a))?
GIVEN `the power` IS A `Power of the directors over officers under s 121(a)` @desc What is the power?
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide?
      `the person to be appointed is of full capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person to be appointed is of full capacity?
      `the power to be delegated is one to do something referred to in subsection 115(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the power to be delegated is one to do something referred to in subsection 115(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the directors have this power over officers` IF `the directors have the power over officers within s 121(a)` `the power` `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` `the person to be appointed is of full capacity` `the power to be delegated is one to do something referred to in subsection 115(3)`

@export May a director be appointed to an office of the corporation (s 121(b))?
GIVEN `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a director be appointed to an office of the corporation` IF `a director may be appointed to an office of the corporation within s 121(b)` `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

@export May I hold two or more offices of the corporation (s 121(c))?
GIVEN `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I hold two or more offices of the corporation` IF `two or more offices of the corporation may be held by the same person within s 121(c)` `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

@export Have I discharged my duty of care as a director or officer (s 122(1))?
GIVEN `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation?
      `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I discharged my duty of care as a director or officer` IF `the director or officer has discharged the duty of care within s 122(1)` `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances`

@export What factors may I consider in acting in the best interests of the corporation (s 122(1.1))?
GIVEN `the person is acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph 122(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph 122(1)(a)?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Factor the directors and officers may consider under s 122(1.1)`
DECIDE `What factors may I consider in acting in the best interests of the corporation` IS `the factors listed that the directors and officers may consider within s 122(1.1)` `the person is acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph 122(1)(a)`

@export Have I complied with the duty to comply with the Act, the articles, the by-laws and any shareholder agreement (s 122(2))?
GIVEN `the person complies with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person complies with the Act?
      `the person complies with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person complies with the regulations?
      `the person complies with the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person complies with the articles?
      `the person complies with the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person complies with the by-laws?
      `the person complies with any unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person complies with any unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with the duty to comply with the Act, the articles, the by-laws and any shareholder agreement` IF `the director or officer has complied with the duty to comply within s 122(2)` `the person complies with the Act` `the person complies with the regulations` `the person complies with the articles` `the person complies with the by-laws` `the person complies with any unanimous shareholder agreement`

@export Does this provision not relieve me of my duties or liability (s 122(3))?
GIVEN `the provision is in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provision is in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution?
      `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with the Act or the regulations?
      `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from liability for a breach of that duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from liability for a breach of that duty?
      `the provision is permitted by subsection 146(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provision is permitted by subsection 146(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision not relieve me of my duties or liability` IF `the provision does not relieve the director or officer within s 122(3)` `the provision is in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution` `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with the Act or the regulations` `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from liability for a breach of that duty` `the provision is permitted by subsection 146(5)`

@export Am I deemed to have consented to the resolution I was present for (s 123(1))?
GIVEN `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors?
      `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes?
      `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned?
      `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have consented to the resolution I was present for` IF `the director is deemed to have consented to the resolution or action within s 123(1)` `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned`

@export Am I still entitled to dissent after I voted for the resolution (s 123(2))?
GIVEN `the director votes for or consents to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director votes for or consents to the resolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still entitled to dissent after I voted for the resolution` IF `the director is entitled to dissent under subsection 123(1) within s 123(2)` `the director votes for or consents to the resolution`

@export Am I treated as having consented to the resolution, as a director who was present (s 123(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors?
      `the director votes for or consents to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director votes for or consents to the resolution?
      `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes?
      `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned?
      `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having consented to the resolution, as a director who was present (s 123(1) and (2))` IF `the present director is treated as having consented within s 123(1) and (2)` `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` `the director votes for or consents to the resolution` `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned`

@export Am I deemed to have consented to a resolution I was absent for (s 123(3))?
GIVEN `the director was present at the meeting at which the resolution was passed or action taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director was present at the meeting at which the resolution was passed or action taken?
      `the date the director became aware of the resolution` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director became aware of the resolution?
      `the date the director dissented, if the director did (yes or no)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a date to give: the date the director dissented, if the director did? (yes or no)
      `the date the director dissented, if the director did (the value)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the director dissented? (if you answered no above, give any date; it is ignored)
      `the director caused a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director caused a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting?
      `the director sent a dissent by registered mail or delivered it to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director sent a dissent by registered mail or delivered it to the registered office of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have consented to a resolution I was absent for` IF `the absent director is deemed to have consented within s 123(3)` `the director was present at the meeting at which the resolution was passed or action taken` `the date the director became aware of the resolution` `the date the director dissented, if the director did as the rule reads it` `the director caused a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting` `the director sent a dissent by registered mail or delivered it to the registered office of the corporation`
    WHERE
        `the date the director dissented, if the director did as the rule reads it` MEANS IF `the date the director dissented, if the director did (yes or no)` THEN JUST `the date the director dissented, if the director did (the value)` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I not liable under ss 118 and 119 because I used reasonable diligence (s 123(4))?
GIVEN `the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not liable under ss 118 and 119 because I used reasonable diligence` IF `the director is not liable under section 118 or 119 and has complied with subsection 122(2) within s 123(4)` `the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances`

@export Have I complied with my duty of care by relying in good faith on financial statements or a professional report (s 123(5))?
GIVEN `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation?
      `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with my duty of care by relying in good faith on financial statements or a professional report` IF `the director has complied with subsection 122(1) by reliance in good faith within s 123(5)` `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person`

@export Have I complied with my duty of care, either directly or by reliance in good faith (s 122(1) and 123(5))?
GIVEN `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation?
      `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances?
      `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation?
      `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with my duty of care, either directly or by reliance in good faith (s 122(1) and 123(5))` IF `the director has complied with the duty of care within s 122(1) and 123(5)` `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances` `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person`

§§ `Indemnity, insurance and pay (ss 124 and 125)`

@export Does the individual fulfil the conditions for an indemnity (s 124(3))?
GIVEN `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request?
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty?
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the individual fulfil the conditions for an indemnity` IF `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3) within s 124(3)` `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

@export May the corporation indemnify me for what I reasonably incurred in a proceeding because of my position (s 124(1))?
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` @desc What is the position of the individual?
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation indemnify me for what I reasonably incurred in a proceeding because of my position` IF `the corporation may indemnify the individual within s 124(1)` `the position of the individual` `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association`

@export May the corporation advance moneys to me for the costs of a proceeding (s 124(2))?
GIVEN `the moneys are for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the moneys are for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection 124(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation advance moneys to me for the costs of a proceeding` IF `the corporation may advance moneys within s 124(2)` `the moneys are for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection 124(1)`

@export Must I repay moneys the corporation advanced to me (s 124(2))?
GIVEN `moneys were advanced to the individual under subsection 124(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that moneys were advanced to the individual under subsection 124(2)?
      `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay moneys the corporation advanced to me` IF `the individual must repay the moneys within s 124(2)` `moneys were advanced to the individual under subsection 124(2)` `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3)`

@export May the corporation, with court approval, indemnify me in a derivative action (s 124(4))?
GIVEN `the court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court approves?
      `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour?
      `the individual is made a party to the action because of the association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is made a party to the action because of the association?
      `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` @desc What is the position of the individual?
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request?
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty?
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation, with court approval, indemnify me in a derivative action` IF `the corporation may with court approval indemnify or advance moneys in the derivative action within s 124(4)` `the court approves` `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` `the individual is made a party to the action because of the association` `the position of the individual` `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

@export May the corporation indemnify me, taking subsections 124(1), (3) and (4) together?
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` @desc What is the position of the individual?
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association?
      `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour?
      `the court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court approves?
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request?
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty?
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation indemnify me, taking subsections 124(1), (3) and (4) together` IF `the corporation may indemnify the individual within s 124(1), (3) and (4)` `the position of the individual` `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association` `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` `the court approves` `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

@export Am I entitled to be indemnified for the cost of defending the proceeding (s 124(5))?
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` @desc What is the position of the individual?
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in connection with the defence of a proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in connection with the defence of a proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the association?
      `the individual was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done?
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request?
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty?
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be indemnified for the cost of defending the proceeding` IF `the individual is entitled to indemnity from the corporation within s 124(5)` `the position of the individual` `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in connection with the defence of a proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the association` `the individual was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done` `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

@export May the corporation buy and maintain insurance for me (s 124(6))?
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` @desc What is the position of the individual?
      `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer of the corporation?
      `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, at the corporation's request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation buy and maintain insurance for me` IF `the corporation may purchase and maintain insurance within s 124(6)` `the position of the individual` `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer of the corporation` `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, at the corporation's request`

@export May I apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity (s 124(7))?
GIVEN `the person is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the corporation?
      `the person is an individual referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an individual referred to in subsection 124(1)?
      `the person is an entity referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an entity referred to in subsection 124(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity` IF `the person may apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity within s 124(7)` `the person is the corporation` `the person is an individual referred to in subsection 124(1)` `the person is an entity referred to in subsection 124(1)`

@export May the court approve the indemnity and make any further order (s 124(7))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application has been made under subsection 124(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court approve the indemnity and make any further order` IF `the court may approve the indemnity and make any further order that it sees fit within s 124(7)` `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

@export Must I give the Director notice of my application (s 124(8))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application has been made under subsection 124(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application` IF `the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 124(8)` `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application (s 124(8))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application has been made under subsection 124(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application` IF `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 124(8)` `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

@export May the court order notice to be given to an interested person (s 124(9))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application has been made under subsection 124(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order notice to be given to an interested person` IF `the court may order notice to be given to an interested person within s 124(9)` `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

@export Am I entitled to appear and be heard as an interested person given notice by the court (s 124(9))?
GIVEN `the court has ordered notice to be given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court has ordered notice to be given to the person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to appear and be heard as an interested person given notice by the court` IF `the interested person is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 124(9)` `the court has ordered notice to be given to the person`

@export May the directors fix my remuneration (s 125)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person whose remuneration the directors may fix under s 125` @desc What is the person?
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors fix my remuneration` IF `the directors may fix the remuneration within s 125` `the person` `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

